ine': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-05-01T01:21:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ed5975e-dbaf-5129-8e28-f58768cec8ea', 'word_count': 209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ed5975e-dbaf-5129-8e28-f58768cec8ea'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, May 1, 2021.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/30/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day-soul-searching-in-israel-after-deadly-stampede-at-religious-site.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, May 1, 2021.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It’s been one blow after another. It’s something we don’t know how to pick ourselves up from.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: Soul-Searching in Israel After Deadly Stampede at Religious Site', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-05-01T01:23:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/a20ce218-9d0b-5993-a597-dfb70b06f5a0', 'word_count': 48, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a20ce218-9d0b-5993-a597-dfb70b06f5a0'}, {'abstract': 'All’s fair in love, war and Ryan McCarty’s Saturday puzzle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/30/crosswords/daily-puzzle-2021-05-01.html', 'snippet': 'All’s fair in love, war and Ryan McCarty’s Saturday puzzle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY PUZZLE — Happy May, everybody! We’re in the lusty height of spring and Ryan McCarty’s grid today has a lot of romantic touches, some verging on bawdy. We are also back on the short stacks, which is fine — a staircase of seven across entries making a sequence that might fit in at a poetry slam. I think the cluing today is reasonably kind, with a few exceptions, although I think I got lucky with a couple of good guesses in the long down entries, which aren’t easy at all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/01/crosswords/01wordplay-water-hazard/01wordplay-water-hazard-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/01/crosswords/01wordplay-water-hazard/01wordplay-water-hazard-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/01/crosswords/01wordplay-water-hazard/01wordplay-water-hazard-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/01/crosswords/01wordplay-water-hazard/01wordplay-water-hazard-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1391, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/01/crosswords/01wordplay-water-hazard/01wordplay-water-hazard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/01/crosswords/01wordplay-water-hazard/01wordplay-water-hazard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/01/crosswords/01wordplay-water-hazard/01wordplay-water-hazard-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Screwballs', 'kicker': 'Wordplay, The CROSSWORD COLUMN', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ties (Apparel)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fortnum & Mason PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarty, Ryan (Crossword Constructor)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-01T02:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caitlin Lovinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d8b678b-a857-5d97-bf03-e341ea740a5e', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d8b678b-a857-5d97-bf03-e341ea740a5e'}, {'abstract': 'A wealth of stores and studios in Connecticut and upstate New York offer lovely handmade wares that you’ll have forever.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/30/t-magazine/craft-shops-connecticut-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'A wealth of stores and studios in Connecticut and upstate New York offer lovely handmade wares that you’ll have forever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I heard that Creel and Gow, the beloved cabinet of antique and handmade curiosities on Manhattan’s Upper East Side, just opened an outpost in Millbrook, N.Y., in order to have more space for its handcrafted furniture and textiles made by artisans in Morocco, where its owners, Jamie Creel and Marco Scarani, live for part of the year, it occurred to me that the area around Millbrook and in nearby Litchfield County, Conn., has become a mecca for craft. Not the chunky or cheeky minimalist Brooklynite-gone-upstate kind of craft, but the kind made by highly skilled longstanding practitioners, whose wares look most at home when paired with fine old patinated things. These sorts of history-friendly creations are the domain of people like Creel and Scarani — shopkeepers (and decorators and antiques dealers) who make keeping a shop seem like an art.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/30/t-magazine/travel/craft-stores-slide-4OE4/craft-stores-slide-4OE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/30/t-magazine/travel/craft-stores-slide-4OE4/craft-stores-slide-4OE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/30/t-magazine/travel/craft-stores-slide-4OE4/craft-stores-slide-4OE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/30/t-magazine/travel/craft-stores-slide-4OE4/craft-stores-slide-4OE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/30/t-magazine/travel/craft-stores-slide-4OE4/craft-stores-slide-4OE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/30/t-magazine/travel/craft-stores-slide-4OE4/craft-stores-slide-4OE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/30/t-magazine/travel/craft-stores-slide-4OE4/craft-store