destal — even if that means destroying their discipline.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, Dan-el Padilla Peralta, a Dominican-born teacher of classics at Princeton, has spoken openly about the harm caused by the discipline’s practitioners in the two millenniums since antiquity — the classical justifications of slavery, race science, colonialism, Nazism and other 20th-century fascisms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sunday Read: ‘He Wants to Save Classics From Whiteness. Can the Field Survive?’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Padilla Peralta, Dan-el', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Princeton University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Daily (Radio Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-02T13:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Podcasts', 'section_name': 'Podcasts', 'subsection_name': 'The Daily', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78ed3f4d-0251-5510-adb1-e2d8cee57710', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78ed3f4d-0251-5510-adb1-e2d8cee57710'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Manisha Jadhav, the chief medical officer at the Group of Tuberculosis Hospitals in Mumbai, died on April 19 in a hospital in that city. She was 51. The cause was complications of Covid-19, her husband said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/02/world/the-chief-medical-officer-at-