ect', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-03T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Katharine Tramontana', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Katharine', 'lastname': 'Tramontana', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff5c7172-b3ed-5c3d-9dfc-2831af6a36f5', 'word_count': 1970, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff5c7172-b3ed-5c3d-9dfc-2831af6a36f5'}, {'abstract': 'Mother’s Day is a time for contemplating the ways we’re connected, through joy and sorrow, across time and across species.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/03/opinion/mothers-day-loss-nature.html', 'snippet': 'Mother’s Day is a time for contemplating the ways we’re connected, through joy and sorrow, across time and across species.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mother’s Day is still nearly a week away, but there are buds on the antique rambling rose that my mother rooted for me from her grandmother’s rose, and it will be in full bloom by Sunday, as it always is on Mother’s Day. My husband will make brunch. Our adult children will come over, and we’ll bring my husband’s 92-year-old father over, too, because he lives for family gatherings and has felt the loss of them more acutely than any of us. We’re all vaccinated now, but we won’t soon forget how it feels to be kept apart.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/03/opinion/03renkl-new/merlin_154213167_814dbe06-2cf6-4945-abaa-76f17b5f6fe3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xla