document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gelles, Andrew Ross Sorkin and Nicholas Kulish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gelles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Ross', 'lastname': 'Sorkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8116b7ad-99b1-50fd-8751-b81056e2c00d', 'word_count': 1220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8116b7ad-99b1-50fd-8751-b81056e2c00d'}, {'abstract': 'Get a taste of Petee’s Pie: The beloved shop now sells its treats frozen and ready to bake, through Goldbelly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/03/dining/petees-pie-company-delivery.html', 'snippet': 'Get a taste of Petee’s Pie: The beloved shop now sells its treats frozen and ready to bake, through Goldbelly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can get a jump on the sour cherry or wild blueberry season with pies from Petee’s Pie Company. Petra Paredez, whose tender, all-butter pastry encloses the judiciously-sweetened fruit, is now selling these online. (Her regular pies, in a wide assortment of flavors, are sold for pickup and local delivery at her shops on the Lower East Side and in Clinton Hill, Brooklyn.) The New York sour cherry, wild blueberry and Hudson Valley apple are shipped frozen, ready-to-bake, from Goldbelly. They come in a six-inch size to indulge two (maybe four if you’re stingy or add lots of ice cream), and a nine-inch size, serving six. The frozen pies go directly from the freezer to the oven and baking takes a good hour. The pies are best allowed to cool before serving, and they can be rewarmed.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/05/dining/28BurnerPie-02/26BurnerPie-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/05/dining/28BurnerPie-02/26BurnerPie-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/05/dining/28BurnerPie-02/26BurnerPie-02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/05/dining/28BurnerPie-02/26BurnerPie-02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1485, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/05/dining/28BurnerPie-02/26BurnerPie-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/05/dining/28BurnerPie-02/26BurnerPie-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/05/dining/28BurnerPie-02/26BurnerPie-02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sour Cherry Pies Straight to Your Door', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Serve: Get a Taste Of Petee’s Pie', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fruit', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Petee's Pie Company (Manhattan, NY, Bakery)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-03T20:49:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5281067d-4d65-592a-8eb1-eb60a9f67bef', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5281067d-4d65-592a-8eb1-eb60a9f67bef'}, {'abstract': 'After a small test release last year, La Crema is making a sauvignon blanc widely available just in time for summer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/03/dining/la-crema-sauvignon-blanc.html', 'snippet': 'After a small test release last year, La Crema is making a sauvignon blanc widely available just in time for summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s never too late to try something new. La Crema, a Sonoma County winery that is known for chardonnay and pinot noir, has introduced a sauvignon blanc. The winery, established in 1979, released the 2019 sauvignon blanc on a limited basis last summer; now the 2020 is widely available. It’s a lovely summer quaff. “The climate and soils of northern Sonoma County are ideal for producing world-class Bordeaux varietals, particularly sauvignon blanc,” said Craig McAllister, the head winemaker. Bordeaux is the operative term here. The wine, in a clear Bordeaux-style bottle, displays more subtle fruit, notably citrus and pineapple, integrated with good acidity, than the grassy herbaceousness typical of sauvignon blancs from other regions. What La Crema has done echoes Sonoma-Cutrer’s introduction in 2015 of its first sauvignon blanc.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 