ection_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': "By ‘The Argument'", 'person': [], 'organization': "The Argument'"}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/04f72b54-d17e-512b-90dd-0dab53192ede', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04f72b54-d17e-512b-90dd-0dab53192ede'}, {'abstract': 'Even a gentle session of leg lifts set off an exaggerated nervous system reaction in older women with rheumatoid arthritis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/05/well/move/arthritis-exercise-women.html', 'snippet': 'Even a gentle session of leg lifts set off an exaggerated nervous system reaction in older women with rheumatoid arthritis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Exercise can feel more difficult and draining than usual if you have rheumatoid arthritis, and it’s not just because of the stiff and painful joints caused by this autoimmune disorder. In a groundbreaking new experiment involving older women and exercise, researchers found that even a gentle session of leg lifts set off an exaggerated nervous system reaction in those with rheumatoid arthritis. Light exercise also negatively affected the inner workings of their muscles and blood vessels.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/arts/05sci-well-physed-autoimmune/05sci-well-physed-autoimmune-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/11/arts/05sci-well-physed-autoimmune/05sci-well-physed-autoimmune-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/arts/05sci-well-physed-autoimmune/05sci-well-physed-autoimmune-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'c