inal': 'By James Poniewozik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Poniewozik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/988a23e7-31b3-53a1-bb34-766f47cded1d', 'word_count': 1363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/988a23e7-31b3-53a1-bb34-766f47cded1d'}, {'abstract': 'A child laid to rest 78,000 years ago yields clues to early human burials in East Africa.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/05/science/earliest-human-burial-africa.html', 'snippet': 'A child laid to rest 78,000 years ago yields clues to early human burials in East Africa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Researchers have identified the earliest known human burial in Africa at Panga ya Saidi, a cave near the Kenyan coast. A child, probably a boy of about 2-1/2 to 3 years old, was placed in a pit about 78,000 years ago, laid carefully on his side, curled up, likely with some kind of pillow under his head.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/science/05TB-BURIAL1/05TB-BURIAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/11/science/05TB-BURIAL1/05TB-BURIAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/science/05TB-BURIAL1/05TB-BURIAL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/science/05TB-BURIAL1/05TB-BURIAL1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 's