agement,” a romance novel about a brilliant undercover agent and her smoking-hot colleague — while a student at Yale Law School. Eager to keep her worlds separate, she used the nom de plume Selena Montgomery, a homage to the “Bewitched” actress Elizabeth Montgomery.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/09/arts/09stacey-abrams1/09stacey-abrams1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/09/arts/09stacey-abrams1/09stacey-abrams1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/09/arts/09stacey-abrams1/09stacey-abrams1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/09/arts/09stacey-abrams1/09stacey-abrams1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/09/arts/09stacey-abrams1/09stacey-abrams1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/09/arts/09stacey-abrams1/09stacey-abrams1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/09/arts/09stacey-abrams1/09stacey-abrams1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stacey Abrams Contains Multitudes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Star Multitasker’s Latest Chapter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abrams, Stacey Y', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'While Justice Sleeps: A Novel (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Personal Profile', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-05T16:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a620c348-c1d1-57b8-8263-d46beccf0443', 'word_count': 1871, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a620c348-c1d1-57b8-8263-d46beccf0443'}, {'abstract': 'The former president’s suspension from Facebook continues\xa0— for now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/05/opinion/facebook-oversight-trump-jan-6.html', 'snippet': 'The former president’s suspension from Facebook continues\xa0— for now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facebook’s Oversight Board on Wednesday upheld the social network’s temporary suspension of Donald Trump but declined to decide when, or whether, that ban should be lifted. The decision dashed the former president’s hopes for a swift reinstatement by a body charged with reviewing the platform’s content moderation practices. But it also sent a message that the scope of the board’s power is limited and that the ultimate responsibility for these questions still lies with Mark Zuckerberg and company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/07/opinion/07Bensinger-inyt/05Renus2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/07/opinion/07Bensinger-inyt/05Renus2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/07/opinion/07Bensinger-inyt/05Renus2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/07/opinion/07Bensinger-inyt/05Renus2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/07/opinion/07Bensinger-inyt/05Renus2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/07/opinion/07Bensinger-inyt/05Renus2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/07/opinion/07Bensinger-inyt/05Renus2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Is Mark Zuckerberg’s Problem. Again.', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Storming of the US Capitol (Jan, 2021)', 'rank': 2, '