-46bdc58999a3', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f19010cf-b89c-5ba2-801a-46bdc58999a3'}, {'abstract': 'Frank Luntz has never felt so gloomy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/06/opinion/sway-kara-swisher-frank-luntz.html', 'snippet': 'Frank Luntz has never felt so gloomy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald Trump isn’t back on Facebook … yet. The platform’s oversight board (set up by Facebook as a “Supreme Court” to which it could punt difficult decisions) upheld a ban on Trump’s account. But the board also said indefinite suspension was “not appropriate.” It gave the company six months to make a final decision on whether Trump can ever return. In short: The court Mark Zuckerberg set up to hide behind has just passed the buck back to Mark Zuckerberg.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/06/opinion/06sway-luntz/06sway-luntz-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/06/opinion/06sway-luntz/06sway-luntz-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/06/opinion/06sway-luntz/06sway-luntz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/06/opinion/06sway-luntz/06sway-luntz-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1619, 'width': 1619, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/06/opinion/06sway-luntz/06sway-luntz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/06/opinion/06sway-luntz/06sway-luntz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/06/opinion/06sway-luntz/06sway-luntz-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘It’s His Own Damn Fault,’ Top G.O.P. Pollster Says of Trump and Facebook', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luntz, Frank I', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oversight Board (Facebook)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-06T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': "By ‘Sway'", 'person': [{'firstname': "Sway'", 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/06a8b5c8-5619-5cf4-a27f-1e36e906e18d', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06a8b5c8-5619-5cf4-a27f-1e36e906e18d'}, {'abstract': "But it's not clear how Facebook should deal with them or how we should deal with Facebook.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/06/opinion/facebook-josh-hawley-trump.html', 'snippet': "But it's not clear how Facebook should deal with them or how we should deal with Facebook.", 'lead_paragraph': 'I was on my iPhone the other day when I heard the first furtive whispers about Big Tech’s silencing of Senator Josh Hawley. Since Jan. 6, when the Missouri Republican was photographed fist-pumping his support for some of the very fine people who would later storm the United States Capitol, Hawley has been all but banished from the media. Other than his frequent appearances on some of the most popular cable news shows in the country, his biting Twitter account, the Instagram account where he posts family snapshots and clips from cable hits, and his YouTube page collecting his nearly every utterance on the Senate floor, Hawley has suffered the worst fate known to a modern American politician: cancellation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/07/opinion/06manjoo-final-print/06manjoo-final-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/07/opinion/06manjoo-final-print/06manjoo-final-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/07/opinion/06manjoo-final-print/06manjoo-final-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/07/opinion/06manjoo-final-print/06manjoo-final-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/07/opinion/06manjoo-final-print/06manjoo-final-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/07/opinion/06manjoo-fi