': 'Dogs that would not be the first choice of many pet owners do better than some of the more agreeable fellows when they have to learn from a stranger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do you have a grumpy dog? It might have some hidden talents.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/science/04TB-DOGS/04TB-DOGS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/11/science/04TB-DOGS/04TB-DOGS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/science/04TB-DOGS/04TB-DOGS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/science/04TB-DOGS/04TB-DOGS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1318, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/science/04TB-DOGS/04TB-DOGS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/11/science/04TB-DOGS/04TB-DOGS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/science/04TB-DOGS/04TB-DOGS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Grumpy Dogs Outperform the Friendlies on Some Learning Tests', 'kicker': 'Trilobites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'They’re Grumpy, but Could Be Willing to Learn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Cognition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Behavior', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oregon State University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Pennsylvania', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Udell, Monique A R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Working Dog Center', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-science', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Budapest (Hungary)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-06T09:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Gorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/841747df-3f01-58cc-9e06-34361b33575b', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/841747df-3f01-58cc-9e06-34361b33575b'}, {'abstract': 'Maps that convince you that we are in a sea of anything but too much suffering are only worthwhile if they inspire a poem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/06/magazine/poem-new-years-eve.html', 'snippet': 'Maps that convince you that we are in a sea of anything but too much suffering are only worthwhile if they inspire a poem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’d never heard of the racial-dot map, another iteration of this country’s obsession with category. As if Crispus Attucks, Black and Native American, didn’t become part of this nation when he took the first bullet in that revolution. Maps that convince you that we are in a sea of anything but too much suffering are only worthwhile if they inspire a poem. Tomás Q. Morín gives us one, and a question: “What story do the dots tell you/about freedom and its promises?” Selected by Reginald Dwayne Betts', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/09/magazine/09mag-poem/09mag-poem-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 552, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/09/magazine/09mag-poem/09mag-poem-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 552}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/09/magazine/09mag-poem/09mag-poem-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 942, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/09/magazine/09mag-poem/09mag-poem-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1506, 'width': 1637, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/09/magazine/09mag-poem/09mag-poem-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/09/magazine/09mag-poem/09mag-poem-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/09/magazine/09mag-poem/09mag-poem-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Poem: New Year’s Eve', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Year’s Eve', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets',