bstract': 'The sugar-laden, high-fat foods we often crave when we are stressed or depressed, as comforting as they are, may be the least likely to benefit our mental health.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/06/well/eat/mental-health-food.html', 'snippet': 'The sugar-laden, high-fat foods we often crave when we are stressed or depressed, as comforting as they are, may be the least likely to benefit our mental health.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As people across the globe grappled with higher levels of stress, depression and anxiety this past year, many turned to their favorite comfort foods: ice cream, pastries, pizza, hamburgers. But studies in recent years suggest that the sugar-laden and high-fat foods we often crave when we are stressed or depressed, as comforting as they may seem, are the least likely to benefit our mental health. Instead, whole foods such as vegetables, fruit, fish, eggs, nuts and seeds, beans and legumes and fermented foods like yogurt may be a better bet.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/06/science/06sci-well-food-mood/06sci-well-food-mood-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1028, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/06/science/06sci-well-food-mood/06sci-well-food-mood-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1028}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/06/science/06sci-well-food-mood/06sci-well-food-mood-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 598, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/06/science/06sci-well-food-mood/06sci-well-food-mood-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1801, 'width': 1051, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_