b88bd', 'word_count': 662, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1009ea6f-99ac-5abf-81da-3192b17b88bd'}, {'abstract': 'NADA House hosts 66 galleries, nonprofits and artist-run spaces arrayed in and around stately officers’ residences. Expect the refreshingly unfamiliar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/06/arts/design/nada-house-2021-governors-island.html', 'snippet': 'NADA House hosts 66 galleries, nonprofits and artist-run spaces arrayed in and around stately officers’ residences. Expect the refreshingly unfamiliar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you want respite from the moneyed, big-name glamour of some of your larger art fairs, you can, in one little trip, leave it all behind; see some relatively untrammeled parts of New York and also revisit the way that many things in the art world begin — that is, in a D.I.Y., grass-roots situation, when people take things into their own hands. If you want V.I.P. services at this event, you’ll have to bring your own; snacks and fluids are recommended and of course sensible shoes. The V.I.P. lounge is a huge greensward graced by tall, regal trees.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/07/arts/06nada-govisland-9/06nada-govisland-9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/07/arts/06nada-govisland-9/06nada-govisland-9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/07/arts/06nada-govisland-9/06nada-govisland-9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/07/arts/06nada-govisland-9/06nada-govisland-9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/07/arts/06nada-govisland-9/merlin_187323927_6598e88e-9ca0-4ab8-b54a-f5eb8f6e8c84-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/07/arts/06nada-govisland-9/merlin_187323927_6598e88e-9ca0-4ab8-b54a-f5eb8f6e8c84-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/07/arts/06nada-govisland-9/merlin_187323927_6598e88e-9ca0-4ab8-b54a-f5eb8f6e8c84-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On Governors Island, Art Interventions Are Everywhere', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Want Glamour? Go Somewhere Else.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Governors Island (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Art Dealers Alliance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-06T18:19:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/891f7340-3398-53da-bed8-6b1300fb4482', 'word_count': 1162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/891f7340-3398-53da-bed8-6b1300fb4482'}, {'abstract': 'Moriondo cited Marie Ulven (who records as girl in red) as an early influence. Both are releasing new albums that showcase frank emotions and more ambitious productions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/06/arts/music/girl-in-red-chloe-moriondo-review.html', 'snippet': 'Moriondo cited Marie Ulven (who records as girl in red) as an early influence. Both are releasing new albums that showcase frank emotions and more ambitious productions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chloe Moriondo began posting YouTube videos in 2014, when she was 11 years old, part of the early waves of young people who built their musical identity on the platform, one bedroom-pop song at a time. She’d been growing up in public for years by August 2019, when she posted a video titled “a ramble about self identity, growth, and being a lesbian.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/06/arts/06album-red-chloe2/06album-red-chloe2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 200, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/06/arts/06album-red-chloe2/06album-red-chloe2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 200}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/06/arts/06album-red-chloe2/06album-red-chloe2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 342, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/06/arts/06album-red-chloe2/06album-red-chloe2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/06/arts/06album-red-chloe2/06album-red-chloe2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/06/arts/06album-red-chloe2/06album-red-chloe2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/06/arts/06album-red-chloe2/06album-red-chloe2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chloe Moriondo and girl in red, Maestros of Growing Pains', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Picks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Showcases From Young Maestros of Emotions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moriondo, Chloe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ulven, Marie (girl in red )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'If I Could Make It Go Quiet (Album)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Blood Bunny (Album)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-06T18:33:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6b5efd8-c38f-5c43-86f7-5d11ca52af4b', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6b5efd8-c38f-5c43-86f7-5d11ca52af4b'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Pollock was best known for dramas inspired by historical events that examined racial tensions and other volatile issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/06/theater/sharon-pollock-dead.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Pollock was best known for dramas inspired by historical events that examined racial tensions and other volatile issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sharon Pollock, an oft-produced Canadian playwright who was known for works that explored Canadian history and identity at a time when few of her contemporaries were doing so, died on April 22 at her home in Calgary, Alberta. She was 85.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/08/obituaries/08Pollock-obit1/merlin_187292739_1b341418-3aaa-4c80-997e-458bc739a375-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 761, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/08/obituaries/08Pollock-obit1/merlin_187292739_1b341418-3aaa-4c80-997e-458bc739a375-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 761}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/08/obituaries/08Pollock-obit1/merlin_187292739_1b341418-3aaa-4c80-997e-458bc739a375-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 808, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/08/obituaries/08Pollock-obit1/merlin_187292739_1b341418-3aaa-4c80-997e-458bc739a375-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1616, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/08/obituaries/08Pollock-obit1/04Pollock1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/08/obituaries/08Pollock-obit1/04Pollock1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,