d Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-08T15:49:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8bd14c4-578e-5770-91b9-5c1f512528f5', 'word_count': 1222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8bd14c4-578e-5770-91b9-5c1f512528f5'}, {'abstract': 'Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon drop us off in the Paleolithic wilderness with our mothers, but of course everything turns out fine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/08/crosswords/variety-acrostic.html', 'snippet': 'Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon drop us off in the Paleolithic wilderness with our mothers, but of course everything turns out fine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ACROSTIC — Happy Mother’s Day! I just got my second dose of vaccine and read Margaret Renkl’s Mother’s Day essay in short order, so I’m feeling a bit weepy. These are emotional times! Thank goodness we have Team Cox/Rathvon to put things into a macrocosmic perspective on humanity and motherhood, courtesy of a passage from “Mothers and Others: The Evolutionary Origins of Mutual Understanding,” by Sarah Blaffer Hrdy, an evolutionary anthropologist. The excerpt describes societal guidance for early people — hunter-gatherers — laid down by the matriarchs of the group: selflessness, congeniality, generosity, humbleness. After you finish it, you’ll think to yourself: “Well, of course that’s how society should work. I knew that already.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Acrostic', 'kicker': 'SUNDAY VARIETY COLUMN', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Mother's Day", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hrdy, Sarah Blaffer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rathvon, Henry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cox, Emily (Crossword Constructor)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-08T16:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caitlin Lovinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c7f8540-2c14-5aa5-b2a2-295af6e68118', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c7f8540-2c14-5aa5-b2a2-295af6e68118'}, {'abstract': 'Most of the debris burned up on re-entry Sunday morning, China said. The head of NASA accused it of “failing to meet responsible standards.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/08/science/china-rocket-reentry-falling-long-march-5b.html', 'snippet': 'Most of the debris burned up on re-entry Sunday morning, China said. The head of NASA accused it of “failing to meet responsible standards.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Debris from a large Chinese rocket landed in the Indian Ocean near the Maldives early Sunday morning, China’s space administration announced. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/08/science/08CHINAROCKET1/08CHINAROCKET1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/08/science/08CHINAROCKET1/08CHINAROCKET1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/08/science/08CHINAROCKET1/08CHINAROCKET1-jum