+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Giulia McDonnell Nieto del Rio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Giulia', 'middlename': 'Mcdonnell', 'lastname': 'Nieto', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a495cb3-937d-5114-b975-a85cf2452244', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a495cb3-937d-5114-b975-a85cf2452244'}, {'abstract': '“The recording angel of the common soldier,” she chronicled the war in seven books from the soldiers’ perspective, drawing on 600 interviews with veterans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/08/books/lyn-macdonald-dead.html', 'snippet': '“The recording angel of the common soldier,” she chronicled the war in seven books from the soldiers’ perspective, drawing on 600 interviews with veterans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mistakenly, they called it the war to end all wars, a grinding collision of empires and nations from 1914 to 1918 that robbed the young of their youth in the mud-bound reaches of Flanders, the Somme and many other fields of battle. Its course and impact inspired a vast canon of military history and increasingly bleak verse from the trenches.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/12/obituaries/07MacDonald1/merlin_187365495_9bcddd92-b9ab-42d1-896b-b5f8a94f9040-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/12/obituaries/07MacDonald1/merlin_187365495_9bcddd92-b9ab-42d1-896b-b5f8a94f9040-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/12/obituaries/07MacDonald1/merlin_187365495_9bcd