ajor': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sheep', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buddhism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Migrants (Environmental)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-10T09:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maxim Babenko', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maxim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Babenko', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96330ae3-248c-5650-a737-5b34de0fc1de', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96330ae3-248c-5650-a737-5b34de0fc1de'}, {'abstract': 'Though they’ve been prized since the dawn of civilization around the world, these natural elixirs have now taken on an almost religious aura for wellness types.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/10/t-magazine/essential-oils-skin-care.html', 'snippet': 'Though they’ve been prized since the dawn of civilization around the world, these natural elixirs have now taken on an almost religious aura for wellness types.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT IS INDIFFERENT to beauty, this ragged tree that disdains soil and grows among the rocks, under bald sun and lashing winds, feeding on difficulty. Short as trees go, it has a hunkered-down look, its branches starting low to the ground and crooking and knotting as they rise. The most prized species make their home in the gullies and wadis of Dhofar in southern Oman and Hadhramaut in war-torn eastern Yemen, and along the cliffs and scarps of the Cal Madow mountains in Somaliland, whose 1991 declaration of independence from Somalia has gone unrecognized by the rest of the world. The Indigenous people of these regions brave snakes and scorpions to climb the trees and press a knife to the papery bark, just enough to break through the green skin beneath. Wounded, the tree begins to ooze, trying to heal itself, its viscous tears hardening into a resin that has been sought after and suffered over for nearly 5,000 years.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '35', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-QE42/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-QE42-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-QE42/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-QE42-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-QE42/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-QE42-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-QE42/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-QE42-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-QE42/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-QE42-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-QE42/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-QE42-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-QE42/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-QE42-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Botanical Oils Won Over the West', 'kicker': 'The 2000s', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Anointing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty (Concept)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oils and Fats', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Luxury Goods and Services', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trees and Shrubs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indigenous People', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-10T09:03:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan, Miranda Barnes and Carlos Nazario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Miranda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Carlos', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nazario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2daea15-2461-5ea2-bd80-46a634a25b08', 'word_count': 4990, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2daea15-2461-5ea2-bd80-46a634a25b08'}, {'abstract': 'Anyone who believes themselves to be so.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/10/t-magazine/beauty-transforming-self.html', 'snippet': 'Anyone who believes themselves to be so.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE OF THE indisputable positives of social media has been an expansion in who and what we consider beautiful. (One of the indisputable negatives has been an ever greater commodification of the self, but that’s a different letter altogether.) I am 46, old enough to remember when top models were almost uniformly white, tall and thin, and am still in awe of how, not so very long ago, many of today’s most compelling faces and bodies would never have found a career in fashion at all, rejected before they even tried for being too dark, too small, too large, too queer, too feminine, too masculine. The ability to say “I’m beautiful” — and to really, truly believe it — may not be a fundamental right, but it, too, is revolutionary in its way, reflective of contemporary upheavals in how we perceive race, gender, sexuality, ability and size. Who gets to be beautiful now? Anyone who believes themselves to be so.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-makeup-slide-DGDE-copy/10tmag-makeup-slide-DGDE-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-makeup-slide-DGDE-copy/10tmag-makeup-slide-DGDE-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-makeup-slide-DGDE-copy/10tmag-makeup-slide-DGDE-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-makeup-slide-DGDE-copy/10tmag-makeup-slide-DGDE-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 810, 'width': 1215, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-makeup-slide-DGDE-copy/10tmag-makeup-slide-DGDE-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-makeup-slide-DGDE-copy/10tmag-makeup-slide-DGDE-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-makeup-slide-DGDE-copy/10tmag-makeup-slide-DGDE-copy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Gets to Be Beautiful Now?', 'kicker': 'Letter from the Editor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Look at Me', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty (Concept)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gender', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-10T09:03:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hanya Yanagihara', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yanagihara', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e9ef442-7bf8-5c7e-a2c6-6fa6c2b8ff21', 'word_count': 621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e9ef442-7bf8-5c7e-a2c6-6fa6c2b8ff21'}, {'abstract': 'At the end of the last century, advances in weaves, wigs and other innovations allowed for a new degree of autonomy — and fun.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/10/t-magazine/black-hair-weaves-wigs.html', 'snippet': 'At the end of the last century, advances in weaves, wigs and other innovations allowed for a new degree of autonomy — and fun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN FEBRUARY 1994, Ellin LaVar, then a 32-year-old Manhattan hairstylist, went to a client’s house in Mendham, N.J., for a home appointment. In the kitchen, she prepared the woman’s hair for a wash by removing the extensions that she had previously put in, using her shears to snip the tiny stitches that fastened the wefts — individual strands of hair that are sewn together to create extensions — to her client’s cornrows. Once she had taken those out, LaVar began to unravel the minuscule braids she had plaited months before, starting at the nape. Using her fingers, she carefully unwound them section by section, until all that was left was the woman’s natural hair. After her client took a shower in one of her four bathrooms, LaVar blow-dried her hair and, over the next hour, once again braided each section of the soft hair into thin cornrows. The woman’s hair was naturally fine and, because she often attended events, she was accustomed to this laborious, time-consuming process.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '62', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-XGFU/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-XGFU-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-XGFU/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-XGFU-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-XGFU/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-XGFU-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-XGFU/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-XGFU-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-XGFU/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-XGFU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-XGFU/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-XGFU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/10/t-magazine/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-XGFU/10tmag-beautytoppers-slide-XGFU-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Joy of Black Hair', 'kicker': 'The 1990s', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Whoever She Wants to Be', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'n