mage than the gillnet, which entangles and kills at least 400,000 seabirds each year.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/science/10TB-BUOYS1/10TB-BUOYS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/11/science/10TB-BUOYS1/10TB-BUOYS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/science/10TB-BUOYS1/10TB-BUOYS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/science/10TB-BUOYS1/10TB-BUOYS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/science/10TB-BUOYS1/10TB-BUOYS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/11/science/10TB-BUOYS1/10TB-BUOYS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/science/10TB-BUOYS1/10TB-BUOYS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Birds and the Buoys: Using Googly Eyes to Avert Extinction', 'kicker': 'Trilobites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scared Safe: To Protect Seabirds, a Strawless Scarecrow Takes Sail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Innovation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Society Open Science (Journal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-science', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-animals', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-10T14:01:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdab92ab-be17-56c9-87e4-8bd6ade87f1a', 'word_count': 662, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdab92ab-be17-56c9-87e4-8bd6ade87f1a'}, {'abstract': 'Take a long walk to space out about food — then head home and make Vietnamese caramel pork and eggs, seis leches cake, or whatever else came to mind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/10/dining/flourishing-in-the-kitchen.html', 'snippet': 'Take a long walk to space out about food — then head home and make Vietnamese caramel pork and eggs, seis leches cake, or whatever else came to mind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. How are you? I drove out to the woods the other day before dawn and was in them as the sun started its ascent. I walked in silence that was not silent at all: bird calls; wind in the canopy; the splash of my boots in a puddle. I was hungry as I walked but not unpleasantly so. I thought about breakfast possibilities, about scrambled eggs and buttered toast, yogurt with a drizzle of maple syrup, crisp bacon, pickled herring. There I was for about an hour, a child of the city deep into nature, thinking about diners and coffee carts and appetizing stores. For the first time in more than a year, I didn’t think about the pandemic at all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/03/dining/29Tetrex1-thit/merlin_182848551_2fdf06bd-bd66-4a69-932b-ac804f983dcc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/02/03/dining/29Tetrex1-thit/merlin_182848551_2fdf06bd-bd66-4a69-932b-ac804f983dcc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/03/dining/29Tetrex1-thit/merlin_182848551_2fdf06bd-bd66-4a69-932b-ac804f983dcc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/03/dining/29Tetrex1-thit/merlin_182848551_2fdf06bd-bd66-4a69-932b-ac804f983dcc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/03/dining/29Tetrex1-thit/29Tetrex1-thit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/02/03/dining/29Tetrex1-thit/29Tetrex1-thit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/02/03/dining/29Tetrex1-thit/29Tetrex1-thit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop