': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shira Ovide', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shira', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ovide', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffc27f86-510c-591a-82a6-7333cf9d0758', 'word_count': 1226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffc27f86-510c-591a-82a6-7333cf9d0758'}, {'abstract': 'The Colonial Pipeline shutdown has exposed vulnerabilities in the nation’s energy infrastructure and raised concerns about fuel supplies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/10/business/colonial-oil-pipeline.html', 'snippet': 'The Colonial Pipeline shutdown has exposed vulnerabilities in the nation’s energy infrastructure and raised concerns about fuel supplies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An oil and gas pipeline system that was forced to shut down on Friday after a ransomware attack is not expected to be “substantially” restored until the end of the week, its operator, Colonial Pipeline, said on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/09/lens/09supplies/merlin_187486854_9e8f60ee-9c5e-4ce1-b0a7-e36855f4a656-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/09/lens/09supplies/merlin_187486854_9e8f60ee-9c5e-4ce1-b0a7-e36855f4a656-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/09/lens/09supplies/merlin_187486854_9e8f60ee-9c5e-4ce1-b0a7-e36855f4a656-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/09/lens/09supplies/merlin_187486854_9e8f60ee-9c5e-4ce1-b0a7-e36855f4a656