ter/honduras-ciudad-oscura.html', 'snippet': 'Back in Honduras for the first time in a decade, a critic finds hopefulness in a city’s cultural ferment — including an energetic theater troupe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On March 12, 2020, I went to an afternoon movie. I was struck by the heavy feeling in Midtown; people looked less determined, more afraid. There were interminable lines inside the drugstores, and at the IMAX theater that seats more than 4,000 people, there was me and a stranger who walked in during the previews.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/09/arts/09solis1/merlin_187322604_4615c584-c3b0-4ee4-825c-2dc63add1df9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/09/arts/09solis1/merlin_187322604_4615c584-c3b0-4ee4-825c-2dc63add1df9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/09/arts/09solis1/merlin_187322604_4615c584-c3b0-4ee4-825c-2dc63add1df9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/09/arts/09solis1/merlin_187322604_4615c584-c3b0-4ee4-825c-2dc63add1df9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/09/arts/09solis1/09solis1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/09/arts/09solis1/09solis1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/09/arts/09solis1/09solis1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Surprising First Live Show, in the Hometown I Once Fled', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Live Show In the Town I Once Fled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Honduras', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'La Ciudad Oscura (Play)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Casa del Teatro Memorias', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-11T18:51:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jose Solís', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jose', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Solís', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a51b4b1e-baf9-5764-a4ef-46b18702b2b1', 'word_count': 1180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a51b4b1e-baf9-5764-a4ef-46b18702b2b1'}, {'abstract': 'He favored phonics to teach reading and grouping students with different aptitudes rather than by age or grade.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/11/education/robert-slavin-dead.html', 'snippet': 'He favored phonics to teach reading and grouping students with different aptitudes rather than by age or grade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert E. Slavin, a sociologist whose research into how children learn helped shift the emphasis in classrooms across the country toward teaching reading through phonics, mixing students of different aptitudes rather than educating them on separate tracks, and testing them for vision and other factors that could a