sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-05-13T18:59:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbdce729-9aa6-5d1a-b663-dc4e948ac1d5', 'word_count': 4681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbdce729-9aa6-5d1a-b663-dc4e948ac1d5'}, {'abstract': 'Reviving higher education in America requires a holistic solution that ends student debt and restores  dignity to educators.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/13/opinion/community-college-student-debt-sanders.html', 'snippet': 'Reviving higher education in America requires a holistic solution that ends student debt and restores  dignity to educators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last 40 years have seen an ever-widening income gap between those with college degrees and those without. Over that interval, incomes have soared for those with advanced degrees and declined for those with high-school diplomas or less. As a result, the route to economic security for young people depends increasingly on access to higher education. Yet it keeps getting more expensive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/13/opinion/13sesankaradair/13sesankaradair-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/13/opinion/13sesankaradair/13sesankaradair-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/13/opinion/13sesankaradair/13sesankaradair-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',