rol of their computers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/13/us/politics/biden-colonial-pipeline-ransomware.html', 'snippet': 'The payment clears the way for gas to begin flowing again, but it risks emboldening other criminal groups to take American companies hostage by seizing control of their computers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The operator of a critical fuel pipeline on the East Coast paid extortionists roughly 75 Bitcoin — or nearly $5 million — to recover its stolen data, according to people briefed on the transaction, clearing the way for gas to begin flowing again but complicating President Biden’s efforts to deter future attacks.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/13/us/politics/13dc-colonial-1/merlin_187705431_6a34ac6e-3159-4713-a157-b532fda6fd80-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 339, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/13/us/politics/13dc-colonial-1/merlin_187705431_6a34ac6e-3159-4713-a157-b532fda6fd80-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 339}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/13/us/politics/13dc-colonial-1/merlin_187705431_6a34ac6e-3159-4713-a157-b532fda6fd80-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 578, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/13/us/politics/13dc-colonial-1/merlin_187705431_6a34ac6e-3159-4713-a157-b532fda6fd80-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1155, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/13/us/politics/13dc-colonial-1/merlin_187705431_6a34ac6e-3159-