021-05-16T15:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Letters', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/d030c7f8-0531-5256-9ec0-ae76d6696378', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d030c7f8-0531-5256-9ec0-ae76d6696378'}, {'abstract': 'We need strong laws and clear regulations to shed light on this megapowerful sector of the global economy. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/16/opinion/commodity-glencore-congo-biden.html', 'snippet': 'We need strong laws and clear regulations to shed light on this megapowerful sector of the global economy. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the final days of Donald Trump’s presidency, all eyes in Washington were on the unprecedented second impeachment of a sitting president after the riot on Capitol Hill. No one noticed when, on Jan. 15, the Treasury quietly eased sanctions on a man it previously described as profiting from “corruption and misconduct.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/18/opinion/01blasfarchy--03/01blasfarchy--03-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/18/opinion/01blasfarchy--03/01blasfarchy--03-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/18/opinion/01blasfarchy--03/01blasfarchy--03-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/18/opinion/01blasfarchy--03/01blasfarchy--03-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'su