eptember, allowing President Donald J. Trump to name her successor and shift the Supreme Court to the right.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/us/politics/17dc-bar/merlin_187604724_938d9ec2-7921-4491-a3f2-baa9e122827f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/17/us/politics/17dc-bar/merlin_187604724_938d9ec2-7921-4491-a3f2-baa9e122827f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/us/politics/17dc-bar/merlin_187604724_938d9ec2-7921-4491-a3f2-baa9e122827f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/us/politics/17dc-bar/merlin_187604724_938d9ec2-7921-4491-a3f2-baa9e122827f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/us/politics/17dc-bar/merlin_187604724_938d9ec2-7921-4491-a3f2-baa9e122827f-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/17/us/politics/17dc-bar/merlin_187604724_938d9ec2-7921-4491-a3f2-baa9e122827f-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/us/politics/17dc-bar/merlin_187604724_938d9ec2-7921-4491-a3f2-baa9e122827f-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge