weighty volume with information on vegetables both common and obscure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/17/dining/the-chefs-garden-vegetable-cookbook.html', 'snippet': '“The Chef’s Garden” is a weighty volume with information on vegetables both common and obscure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lee Jones, an Ohio farmer who famously wears overalls and a red bow tie, runs a family farm that caters to chefs, cultivating the everyday (broccoli) and the less common (cardoons). The farm has an educational adjunct, the Culinary Vegetable Institute, and now, “The Chef’s Garden,” a thick book all about vegetables. Merely leafing its pages results in tidbits of information like this: When spinach is very fresh and you rub the leaves together, “they should squeak.” The massive illustrated volume (640 pages) covers hundreds of vegetables, grouped in categories, with history and advice on growing, buying, storing and using. There are scores of recipes from Jamie Simpson, the institute’s head chef; if you make only one of them it should be the luscious carrot pot roast. The story of the farm mirrors the evolution of vegetable cultivation and consumption over recent decades.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17Burner-book/17Burner-book-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17Burner-book/17Burner-book-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 729}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17Burner-book/17Burner-book-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 844, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17Burner-book/17Burner-book-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1687, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17Burner-book/17Burner-book-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17Burner-book/17Burner-book-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17Burner-book/17Burner-book-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Book That Celebrates Vegetables', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Study: New Book Celebrates All Types of Vegetables', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "The Chef's Garden (Book)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Lee (Farmer)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-17T19:41:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6843dc17-1735-5269-ad5f-7c7a7aa95c2c', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6843dc17-1735-5269-ad5f-7c7a7aa95c2c'}, {'abstract': 'At Santa Carota ranch in Bakersfield, Calif., the livestock is finished on a diet of carrots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/17/dining/santa-carota-beef.html', 'snippet': 'At Santa Carota ranch in Bakersfield, Calif., the livestock is finished on a diet of carrots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Santa Carota beef is raised on a ranch near Bakersfield, Calif. The name of both the meat and the ranch comes from the carrots used by the Pettit family as feed for the animals, which are grass-fed in open pastures but finished on a diet of carrots. The ranch started adding carrots from local farms to the finishing feed in 1989; now it’s all carrots because it liked the results. Chefs, including Wolfgang Puck and Gordon Ramsay, did too, and became regular customers. The beef — available in New York strip, rib-eye, filet mignon, tomahawk and hibachi strips, with other cuts coming soon — is now being sold retail for the first time through Holy Grail Steak Company. Each cut is shipped frozen and is available in a regular grade or prestige, the equivalent of prime. I did not find much difference between the two grades, though the prestige rib-eye was slightly silkier than the regular. All had good beefy flavor.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-beef/17burner-beef-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-beef/17burner-beef-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-beef/17burner-beef-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-beef/17burner-beef-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-beef/17burner-beef-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-beef/17burner-beef-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-beef/17burner-beef-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Carrots Give This Beef Flavor', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sear: Carrots Help Bring  This Beef to Market', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beef', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carrots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-17T19:41:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/830af880-82b9-5207-a7fb-42ca4c8f066a', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/830af880-82b9-5207-a7fb-42ca4c8f066a'}, {'abstract': 'Patagonia Provisions’s latest release, breadfruit crackers and white anchovies, go anywhere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/17/dining/patagonia-provisions.html', 'snippet': 'Patagonia Provisions’s latest release, breadfruit crackers and white anchovies, go anywhere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the trail or around the campfire, you have to eat. And increasingly, Patagonia, the outdoor gear company, can stock your backpack. Its line of responsibly sourced shelf-stable products keeps expanding; most are also worth pantry space at home. Among the latest are crackers made from breadfruit flour — take that, Captain Bligh! The handy, crisp little squares come in three flavors — honey sesame, seeded turmeric and aji molido — ready for a dip or a smear of chèvre. The company has also introduced plump Spanish anchovies seasoned with roasted garlic, or lemon and olive. These are whole fish, more like sardines than the flat, salty strips one thinks of for a Caesar salad. They’re excellent on a tartine, for tapas or even tossed with pasta.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-pat/17burner-pat-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-pat/17burner-pat-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 436}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-pat/17burner-pat-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-pat/17burner-pat-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 983, 'width': 1354, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-pat/17burner-pat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-pat/17burner-pat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-pat/17burner-pat-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Camping or Canapés', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Savor: Patagonia Goodies For Camping or Canapés', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Patagonia Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-17T19:42:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bca44db-730d-5c04-9cb2-52fa8e8fa798', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bca44db-730d-5c04-9cb2-52fa8e8fa798'}, {'abstract': 'A large portion of the purchase price of the Sette’s new collaboration with the designer Anna Polonsky goes toward World Central Kitchen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/17/dining/anna-polonsky-world-central-kitchen.html', 'snippet': 'A large portion of the purchase price of the Sette’s new collaboration with the designer Anna Polonsky goes toward World Central Kitchen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When companies or restaurants say they’re donating a portion of profits to charity, it frequently amounts to a few dollars. But not the Sette, a tableware website from London that is now selling elegant bone-china platters in collaboration with Anna Polonsky of Polonsky & Friends, a design company. Buy the 14-inch oval platter — traced with verses by the poet Sara Teasdale — for $254.25 and $101 will be donated to World Central Kitchen, the nonprofit organization founded by the chef José Andrés that responds to disasters with food. A 16-inch oval platter with a border by Mary Clerté of spring motifs like bunnies and lambs is $303, of which $121.75 is donated to World Central Kitchen.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burnerdish/17burnerdish-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burnerdish/17burnerdish-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burnerdish/17burnerdish-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burnerdish/17burnerdish-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burnerdish/17burnerdish-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burnerdish/17burnerdish-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burnerdish/17burnerdish-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'These Serving Platters Do More', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Present: These Serving Platters Have a Meaningful Reach', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tableware', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Central Kitchen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-17T19:43:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8999573b-ea56-5df6-bc39-3b47387a8a8c', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8999573b-ea56-5df6-bc39-3b47387a8a8c'}, {'abstract': 'A virtual talk later this month through the Museum of Food and Drink celebrates Albanian cooks and their dishes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/17/dining/albanian-cooking.html', 'snippet': 'A virtual talk later this month through the Museum of Food and Drink celebrates Albanian cooks and their dishes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Albanian cuisine — woven from threads of Balkan, Mediterranean and Ottoman traditions — features dishes like stuffed vegetables, phyllo pastries, meatballs and yogurt. For more details transmitted straight from Albania, the Museum of Food and Drink and the Greene Space have organized a virtual 90-minute talk and a cooking demonstration. Representatives from RRNO, a group of Albanian chefs with a mission to preserve and promote the cuisine, will discuss it and demonstrate two recipes at the end.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-talk/17burner-talk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-talk/17burner-talk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-talk/17burner-talk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-talk/17burner-talk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-talk/17burner-talk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-talk/17burner-talk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/19/dining/17burner-talk/17burner-talk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Heart of Albanian Cooking', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Learn: The Heart Of Albanian Cooking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBANIA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Food and Drink (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-17T19:44:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2258a87-9310-5552-9b75-0d1a4b684218', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2258a87-9310-5552-9b75-0d1a4b684218'}, {'abstract': 'Giancarlo Stanton has overcome a slow start to be his team’s second-best hitter. A strained quadriceps muscle will force him to be out until at least May 25.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/17/sports/baseball/giancarlo-stanton-yankees-il.html', 'snippet': 'Giancarlo Stanton has overcome a slow start to be his team’s second-best hitter. A strained quadriceps muscle will force him to be out until at least May 25.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Off to a slow start, the Yankees found their footing over the past several weeks thanks, in part, to an offense led by right fielder Aaron Judge and designated hitter Giancarlo Stanton. With a recent torrid stretch of hitting, Judge was tied for the major-league lead in home runs (12) entering Monday. Hitting in front of him most of the season was Stanton, with the sluggers tied for the team lead at 24 runs batted in.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/sports/17mlb-yankees/merlin_187673088_aba316e2-66f6-442b-ac45-05035013e205-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/17/sports/17mlb-yankees/merlin_187673088_aba316e2-66f6-442b-ac45-05035013e205-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/sports/17