okerage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/18/business/buying-a-home-here-is-how-to-navigate-the-housing-market.html', 'snippet': '', 'lead_paragraph': 'Homes are selling quickly. About half sell in less than a week, usually after multiple offers, said Daryl Fairweather, the chief economist for the Redfin online brokerage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/15/business/14Adviser-illo/14Adviser-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/15/business/14Adviser-illo/14Adviser-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/15/business/14Adviser-illo/14Adviser-illo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/15/business/14Adviser-illo/14Adviser-illo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/15/business/14Adviser-illo/14Adviser-illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/15/business/14Adviser-illo/14Adviser-illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/15/business/14Adviser-illo/14Adviser-illo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Buying a home? Here is how to navigate the housing market.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-05-18T10:58:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98019b96-39ef-5ffd-a553-607eb508a91d', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98019b96-39ef-5ffd-a553-607eb508a91d'}, {'abstract': 'Federal Reserve officials believe low and stable price expectations give them room to heal the job market. But what if outlooks change?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/18/business/how-all-the-talk-about-inflation-could-complicate-matters-for-the-fed.html', 'snippet': 'Federal Reserve officials believe low and stable price expectations give them room to heal the job market. But what if outlooks change?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Turn on the news, scroll through Facebook, or listen to a White House briefing these days and there’s a good chance you’ll catch the Federal Reserve’s least-favorite word: Inflation. If that bubbling popular concern about prices gets too ingrained in America’s psyche, it could spell trouble for the nation’s central bank.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/18/business/17JPdc-inflation2-print/merlin_187686768_6508bc55-0369-4074-ab0d-26eb45074123-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/18/business/17JPdc-inflation2-print/merlin_187686768_6508bc55-0369-4074-ab0d-26eb45074123-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/18/business/17JPdc-inflation2-print/merlin_187686768_6508bc55-0369-4074