middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lumbreras', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brasero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/a3e56b87-9786-5053-af27-faa4768322eb', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/a3e56b87-9786-5053-af27-faa4768322eb'}, {'abstract': 'Modern Love in miniature, featuring reader-submitted stories of no more than 100 words.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/18/style/tiny-modern-love-stories-nothing-my-husband-did-helped.html', 'snippet': 'Modern Love in miniature, featuring reader-submitted stories of no more than 100 words.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The closest thing my daughter, Ella, could get to a pandemic pet was a Venus flytrap (named Venus). Ella won a scholarship to boarding school and left last August. I lit candles for Venus and collected rainwater for her. Taking care of Ella’s fragile plant was as close as I could get to taking care of her. In the winter I thought Venus was dead. No, just dormant. I moved her to a cooler place and waited for spring. And then, a slender stem! A mouth and even teeth coming soon. Who said these girls are fragile? — Sharon Harrigan', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/15/fashion/00MAY-ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO-6/00MAY-ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO-6-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/15/fashion/00MAY-ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO-6/00MAY-ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO-6-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/15/fashion/00MAY-ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO-6/00MAY-ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO-6-jumbo-v2.j