0-years-of-immigration-history-with-the-times-archive.html', 'snippet': 'In this lesson, students will use the New York Times archive to learn about immigration laws from 1882 to 1986. Then they will make connections to today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year marks the 100th anniversary of the first law passed in the United States to establish numerical limits on immigrants entering the country. However, the 1921 Emergency Quota Act was not the first time that the United States had introduced restrictive immigration laws. The 1882 Chinese Exclusion Act prohibited the entry of all laborers from China, and restrictive immigration laws would continue through the 19th and 20th centuries to today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/07/learning/07LODTimesMachineLN/07LODTimesMachineLN-articleLarge.png', 'height': 324, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/07/learning/07LODTimesMachineLN/07LODTimesMachineLN-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 324}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/07/learning/07LODTimesMachineLN/07LODTimesMachineLN-jumbo.png', 'height': 554, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/07/learning/07LODTimesMachineLN/07LODTimesMachineLN-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1038, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/07/learning/07LODTimesMachineLN/07LODTimesMachineLN-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/07/learni