: 'The pandemic may now be in permanent retreat in the U.S.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I want to end this week by showing you two Covid-19 charts. They contain the same message: The pandemic is in retreat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/lens/21ambriefing-promo/17ambriefing-family02-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/17/lens/21ambriefing-promo/17ambriefing-family02-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/lens/21ambriefing-promo/17ambriefing-family02-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/lens/21ambriefing-promo/17ambriefing-family02-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/lens/21ambriefing-promo/17ambriefing-family02-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/17/lens/21ambriefing-promo/17ambriefing-family02-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/lens/21ambriefing-promo/17ambriefing-family02-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Covid on the Run', 'kicker': 'The Morning Newsletter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-05-21T10:22:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a8a9ede-850c-50ec-b974-39b0471103b4', 'word_count': 1457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a8a9ede-850c-50ec-b974-39b0471103b4'}, {'abstract': 'Many of us relied on screens to stay connected and entertained during the restrictions of pandemic life. To break your family or friends’ screen habits, you don’t have to go cold turkey. Instead, practice separating yourself from your phone for periods of time. Some ways to do this: Don’t check any screen until you’ve been up for a half hour. Take a walk or go to lunch without your phone. At dinner, try a “first-to-look” game. Put all phones at the center of the table. The first one to look does the dishes or pays the tab! ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/21/well/pandemic-wellness-tech-break.html', 'snippet': '', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many of us relied on screens to stay connected and entertained during the restrictions of pandemic life. To break your family or friends’ screen habits, you don’t have to go cold turkey. Instead, practice separating yourself from your phone for periods of time. Some ways to do this: Don’t check any screen until you’ve been up for a half hour. Take a walk or go to lunch without your phone. At dinner, try a “first-to-look” game. Put all phones at the center of the table. The first one to look does the dishes or pays the tab! ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/04/well/challenge-no-tech/challenge-no-tech-articleLa