ns', 'value': 'Hashimoto, Seiko (1964- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-21T14:29:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Motoko Rich and Victor Mather', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Motoko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mather', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/793ae87c-b31e-5490-bab8-7fc13f56f0d3', 'word_count': 617, 'uri': 'nyt://article/793ae87c-b31e-5490-bab8-7fc13f56f0d3'}, {'abstract': 'Make a big batch of ranchero sauce for the base of huevos rancheros, or break out the grill for chicken skewers or coffee-rubbed fish.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/21/dining/what-to-cook-this-weekend.html', 'snippet': 'Make a big batch of ranchero sauce for the base of huevos rancheros, or break out the grill for chicken skewers or coffee-rubbed fish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gabrielle Hamilton took a close look at the economics of restaurant brunch this week in The Times, reflecting on the two decades she spent working the shift at Prune, her jewel box of a dining room in the East Village, before putting the place to sleep at the start of the pandemic. It’s a delicious read as it always is when Gabrielle takes to the keyboard — “that 10-burner egg station during a rocking, relentless, 230-covers brunch, holy smokes!” — and reflective, too. If she ever brings her business back, she writes, it won’t be to serve brunch, not in a city where the word has become a verb and the waiters make four times what those cooking the eggs do. She’s already thrown out the pans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/23/magazine/23mag-eat/23mag-eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/23/magazine/23mag-eat/23mag-eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/23/magazine/23mag-eat/23mag-eat-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/23/magazine/23mag-eat/23mag-eat-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/23/magazine/23mag-eat/23mag-eat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/23/magazine/23mag-eat/23mag-eat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/23/magazine/23mag-eat/23mag-eat-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Cook This Weekend', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-05-21T14:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a519c3