 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ali', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Watkins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bde8a37-9215-5617-8771-3b48bf529a82', 'word_count': 953, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bde8a37-9215-5617-8771-3b48bf529a82'}, {'abstract': 'We can criticize Netanyahu and still recognize our allies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/21/opinion/israel-democrats-netanyahu-hamas-nadler.html', 'snippet': 'We can criticize Netanyahu and still recognize our allies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent days, there has been a lot of talk about the Democratic Party’s purportedly changing position on Israel. And reports have emerged contending that two opposing far-edge stances are the Democrats’ so-called real position — one side asserting that Israel should no longer receive U.S. security assistance and another suggesting full-throated, uncritical support of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, no matter how extreme his policies have become. Let me be clear: These oversimplified narratives couldn’t be further from the truth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/24/opinion/24Nadler-Sub-inyt/21Nadler-Sub-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/24/opinion/24Nadler-Sub-inyt/21Nadler-Sub-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/24/opinion/24Nadler-Sub-inyt/21Nadler-Sub-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 747, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/24/opinion/24Nadler-Sub-inyt/21Nadler-Sub-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1495, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/24/opinion/24Nadler-Sub-inyt/21Nadler-Sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/24/opinion/24Nadler-Sub-inyt/21Nadler-Sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/24/opinion/24Nadler-Sub-inyt/21Nadler-Sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Democrats Have Not Changed Their Position on Israel', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestine Liberation Organization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-21T19:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jerrold L. Nadler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jerrold', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Nadler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0449c7e-5b63-5529-b5c1-c824e5fc9b78', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0449c7e-5b63-5529-b5c1-c824e5fc9b78'}, {'abstract': 'Want to increase vaccination rates? Address adults’ fear of needles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/21/opinion/needle-fear-vaccine-covid.html', 'snippet': 'Want to increase vaccination rates? Address adults’ fear of needles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No one likes needles. Of all the barriers to Covid-19 vaccination, fear of needles may seem trivial to overcome. But millions of American adults, not to mention children, still need to be injected to keep themselves and their communities safe. And it’s likely some of them aren’t doing so in part because they fear or just don’t like needles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/21/opinion/21McMurtry-illo/21McMurtry-illo-articleLarge-v11.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/21/opinion/21McMurtry-illo/21McMurtry-illo-articleLarge-v11.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/21/opinion/21McMurtry-illo/21McMurtry-illo-jumbo-v11.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/21/opinion/21McMurtry-illo/21McMurtry-illo-superJumbo-v11.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/21/opinion/21McMurtry-illo/21McMurtry-illo-thumbStandard-v14.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/21/opinion/21McMurtry-illo/21McMurtry-illo-thumbStandard-v14.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/21/opinion/21McMurtry-illo/21McMurtry-illo-thumbLarge-v14.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Needle Fear Is an Underrecognized Vaccination Challenge', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fear (Emotion)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hypodermic Needles and Syringes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-21T19:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. Meghan McMurtry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'Meghan', 'lastname': 'McMurtry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c3d8606-b0a2-5665-a78c-c19e0286f546', 'word_count': 1004, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c3d8606-b0a2-5665-a78c-c19e0286f546'}, {'abstract': 'Even risking our lives during a pandemic doesn’t protect us from racism and sexism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/21/opinion/asian-american-women-doctors-racism-sexism.html', 'snippet': 'Even risking our lives during a pandemic doesn’t protect us from racism and sexism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was near the beginning of the pandemic, in mid-April of 2020, when a stranger spit on me. After apparently taking note of my hospital badge and mask, he announced that even though I was a doctor, I “brought the sickness.” He called me “Hindu,” along with a string of profanities.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/20/opinion/20bhuvaneswar/20bhuvaneswar-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/20/opinion/20bhuvaneswar/20bhuvaneswar-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/20/opinion/20bhuvaneswar/20bhuvaneswar-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/20/opinion/20bhuvaneswar/20bhuvaneswar-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/20/opinion/20bhuvaneswar/20bhuvaneswar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/20/opinion/20bhuvaneswar/20bhuvaneswar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/20/opinion/20bhuvaneswar/20bhuvaneswar-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As a Doctor, I’ve Worked Tirelessly Through the Pandemic. That Hasn’t Stopped the Hate.', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Hate Directed at Me', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asian-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-21T19:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chaya Bhuvaneswar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bhuvaneswar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/57893f6b-c35c-590c-aa2f-5862c451a3ff', 'word_count': 1100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57893f6b-c35c-590c-aa2f-5862c451a3ff'}, {'abstract': 'At least 27 people were arrested after demonstrations in Times Square and the Diamond District in Midtown Manhattan. Several lawmakers have denounced the clashes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/21/nyregion/times-square-protest-diamond-district.html', 'snippet': 'At least 27 people were arrested after demonstrations in Times Square and the Diamond District in Midtown Manhattan. Several lawmakers have denounced the clashes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several New York City elected officials on Friday denounced clashes that took place between pro-Israeli and pro-Palestinian protesters in Midtown Manhattan, leading to more than two dozen arrests and at least two people being hospitalized.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/21/nyregion/21nyprotest/21nyprotest-articleLarge.jpg', 'height