weekend.html', 'snippet': 'SPF, summer reading, and to-go cocktails.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome. It’s getting to be last-day-of-school sunny and warm here in the Northeastern United States. We’re on the verge of summer again. Last May, a return to normal life felt almost impossible to ponder. This year, while we still have many questions about Covid-19 (What do parents need to know about kids and vaccines? Why did the C.D.C. change its advice on masks?), we’re making space for more before-timesish questions too (How much SPF is enough? What should I read this summer? Which beers does Eric Asimov recommend for a hot day?).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/21/multimedia/21At-Home-Newsletter/21At-Home-Newsletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/21/multimedia/21At-Home-Newsletter/21At-Home-Newsletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/21/multimedia/21At-Home-Newsletter/21At-Home-Newsletter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/21/multimedia/21At-Home-Newsletter/21At-Home-Newsletter-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1166, 'width': 1750, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/21/multimedia/21At-Home-Newsletter/21At-Home-Newsletter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/21/multimedia/21At-Home-Newsletter/21At-Home-Newsletter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/21/multimedia/21At-Home-Newsletter/21At-Home-Newsletter-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Do This Weekend', 'kicker': 'At Home Newsletter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-21T20:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'AtHome', 'section_name': 'At Home', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Kirsch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kirsch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ef0bb95-3b35-5426-a73d-65e42ee0b3ff', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ef0bb95-3b35-5426-a73d-65e42ee0b3ff'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Schenkar was also known for experimental plays. In one, a reimagining of the Red Riding Hood story, Grandma was a butcher.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/21/books/joan-schenkar-dead.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Schenkar was also known for experimental plays. In one, a reimagining of the Red Riding Hood story, Grandma was a butcher.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joan Schenkar, who started her career as a playwright but switched to biography, producing an especially well-regarded take on a complex literary figure in 2009 with her book “The Talented Miss Highsmith: The Secret Life and Serious Art of Patricia Highsmith,” died on May 5 in Paris. She was 78.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'imag