ne, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders and Memorandums', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'internal-essential', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-22T14:38:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adeel Hassan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adeel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hassan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0afcafa0-8c35-554b-a8be-e89fdbc9fa16', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0afcafa0-8c35-554b-a8be-e89fdbc9fa16'}, {'abstract': 'The Big Pharma drug model is inefficient and unsustainable. There is an alternative.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/22/opinion/drug-developed-covid-19-pill.html', 'snippet': 'The Big Pharma drug model is inefficient and unsustainable. There is an alternative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — Nine years ago, Dr. Dennis Liotta, a professor of organic chemistry at Emory University, set out to change the way drugs are developed for so-called neglected diseases — those that primarily affect populations in poorer countries and for which there exist few, if any, safe and effective treatments.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Race for a Covid-19 Pill, a Little Lab Plays a Big Role', 'kicker': 'guest essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clinical Trials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Emory University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liotta, Dennis C', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-22T15:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Adams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Adams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/36e31470-a773-5420-8409-5fb8c6589c1c', 'word_count': 1350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36e31470-a773-5420-8409-5fb8c6589c1c'}, {'abstract': 'As we emerge from the pandemic, we should welcome a wider range of physical connection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/22/opinion/friends-holding-hands-touch.html', 'snippet': 'As we emerge from the pandemic, we should welcome a wider range of physical connection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was crossing a vast, chaotic Dar es Salaam intersection one evening when a pastor I’d known just a few days took my hand. He held on until we crossed the street and reached a more tranquil path. It was hard to shake my American interpretation of this gesture — I was used to hand-holding happening only between lovers, or parents and children. But I knew he meant it as an expression of care and mark of the connection we’d formed over multiple days collaborating on some research of mine. And I started to wonder — why shouldn’t Americans hold hands more freely?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/22/opinion/22broadway/22broadway-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/22/opinion/22broadway/22broadway-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/22/opinion/22broadway/22broadway-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/22/opinion/22broadway/22broadway-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/22/opinion/22broadway/22broadway-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/22/opinion/22broadway/22broadway-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/22/opinion/22broadway/22broadway-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Americans, It’s Time to Get Comfortable With Platonic Touch', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Get Comfortable With Platonic Touch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Touch (Sense)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greeting Gestures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hugging', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-22T15:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna Broadway', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Broadway', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/12c0f577-022d-577c-9e25-c73b06dc8042', 'word_count': 1037, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12c0f577-022d-577c-9e25-c73b06dc8042'}, {'abstract': 'Fiame Naomi Mata’afa was set to be sworn in Monday as the country’s first new prime minister in 22 years, until the head of state suspended Parliament.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/22/world/asia/samoa-election-crisis.html', 'snippet': 'Fiame Naomi Mata’afa was set to be sworn in Monday as the country’s first new prime minister in 22 years, until the head of state suspended Parliament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUCKLAND, New Zealand — The Pacific island nation of Samoa hurtled toward a constitutional crisis on Saturday, when the country’s head of state announced that he was suspending Parliament just two days before it was scheduled to swear in the country’s first new prime minister in more than two decades.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/22/world/22SAMOA-ELECTION01/merlin_186643044_5baa3674-4622-4e4e-b3ec-64fb4ab4170a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/22/world/22SAMOA-ELECTION01/merlin_186643044_5baa3674-4622-4e4e-b3ec-64fb4ab4170a