'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-23T03:59:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'AtHome', 'section_name': 'At Home', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Levine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Levine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d8e915b-6125-5454-b7c7-b9f30ebdb7cd', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d8e915b-6125-5454-b7c7-b9f30ebdb7cd'}, {'abstract': 'Professional golfers worry about sustaining peak form, but say that scheduling four championships April through July is good for the game, and anyone who gets on a roll.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/23/sports/golf/four-major-tournaments-in-four-months-is-a-lot-of-important-golf.html', 'snippet': 'Professional golfers worry about sustaining peak form, but say that scheduling four championships April through July is good for the game, and anyone who gets on a roll.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KIAWAH ISLAND, S.C. — This is just the second time in the modern era of men’s professional golf that the sport’s four major championships will be contested in consecutive months, one each from April through July. The schedule was similar in 2019 when, after years of deliberation, the P.G.A. Championship opted to move to May, from its long standing date in mid-August.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/23/sports/23golf-schedule1-print/merlin_188106708_2883329c-99b0-47a0-856c-9ed5079be834-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/23/sports/23golf-schedule1-print/merlin_188106708_2883329c-99b0-47a0-856c-9ed5079be834-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {