entive Medicine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ultrasonic Imaging and Sonograms', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transfusions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sickle Cell Anemia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institutes of Health', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-23T22:17:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Kolata and Ilana Panich-Linsman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolata', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ilana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Panich-Linsman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e87281c3-9700-5074-bf13-812310a39540', 'word_count': 2620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e87281c3-9700-5074-bf13-812310a39540'}, {'abstract': 'For once, entertainers gather and judges bestow awards, but big-brand marketing is conspicuously absent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/23/fashion/eurovision-fashion.html', 'snippet': 'For once, entertainers gather and judges bestow awards, but big-brand marketing is conspicuously absent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is an uncomfortable reality of the modern communal spectacle that more often than not, when it comes to a major award show or performance extravaganza or even sporting event, marketing has overwhelmed personal expression — at least when it comes to the clothes. Red carpets are a big business for public personalities, and fear of looking silly an equally powerful deterrent. Brands have swooped in to exploit that tension to their own ends.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/23/arts/23eurovision-fashion2/merlin_188163840_700e4081-c725-4710-982b-3db3c8ee6647-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/23/arts/23eurovision-fashion2/merlin_188163840_700e4081-c725-4710-982b-3db3c8ee6647-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/23/arts/23eurovision-fashion2/merlin_188163840_700e4081-c725-4710-982b-3db3c8ee6647-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/23/arts/23eurovision-fashion2/merlin_188163840_700e4081-c725-4710-982b-3db3c8ee6647-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/23/arts/23eurovision-fashion2/23eurovision-fashion2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/23/arts/23eurovision-fashion2/23eurovision-fashion2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/23/arts/23eurovision-fashion2/23eurovision-fas