'', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6176867a-2956-531c-bb09-ec6a92b49b65', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6176867a-2956-531c-bb09-ec6a92b49b65'}, {'abstract': 'New York Wine Events has added more private tours of wineries in the North Fork. There are trips planned to the Hudson Valley, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/24/dining/wine-tours-long-island.html', 'snippet': 'New York Wine Events has added more private tours of wineries in the North Fork. There are trips planned to the Hudson Valley, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York Wine Events, which conducts day trips to the wine country of Long Island and Hudson Valley, has expanded its schedule this year, a smart move considering that people who are resuming travel as pandemic restrictions ease are doing so closer to home. Custom trips for groups of two or more are now available daily through the end of the year. Round trip transportation can be arranged from a pickup point in any of the city’s boroughs, plus Long Island for North Fork wineries or Westchester and Rockland Counties for the Hudson Valley. There will be a sommelier present as the group visits two wineries and samples four to five wines at each stop. A visit to a farm stand is included. Participants must be at least 21 years old and tours have to be booked at least 48 hours in advance. The tours go rain or shine, follow any pandemic protocols and start at $159 per person.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/26/dining/24burner-wine/24burner-tour-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/26/dining/24burner-wine/24burner-tour-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/26/dining/24burner-wine/24burner-tour-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/26/dining/24burner-wine/24burner-tour-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/26/dining/24burner-wine/24burner-tour-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/26/dining/24burner-wine/24burner-tour-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/26/dining/24burner-wine/24burner-tour-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wine Tours Ramp Up on Long Island', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Tour: Leave Town and Toast New York Wine Country', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Winship Media LLC (New York Wine Events)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-24T21:07:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19c3a933-fc89-561e-876e-2280ca238265', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19c3a933-fc89-561e-876e-2280ca238265'}, {'abstract': 'Patrick McMurray, a champion shucker, will lead an hourlong course in oyster shucking next month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/24/dining/oyster-shucking-class.html', 'snippet': 'Patrick McMurray, a champion shucker, will lead an hourlong course in oyster shucking next month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oyster expertise in an hour, in a virtual class, is promised by Food Island Partnership, the organization that promotes shellfish from Prince Edward Island, Canada. Patrick McMurray, a champion shucker, will guide the audience in a free event that covers buying and storing oysters, shucking them (with oysters and tools you can purchase in advance to get ready), serving and appreciating them. In addition to oysters and knives, you can also buy Mr. McMurray’s book, “The Oyster Companion.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/26/dining/24burner-shell/merlin_187959384_6297f677-c069-41f4-a3ec-e550e53ad3f8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 875, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/26/dining/24burner-shell/merlin_187959384_6297f677-c069-41f4-a3ec-e550e53ad3f8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 875}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/26/dining/24burner-shell/merlin_187959384_6297f677-c069-41f4-a3ec-e550e53ad3f8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 703, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/26/dining/24burner-shell/merlin_187959384_6297f677-c069-41f4-a3ec-e550e53ad3f8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 197