'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/20/opinion/opdoc-bobofthepark/opdoc-bobofthepark-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bob of the Park', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birdwatching', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeCandido, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-25T19:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Sumner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sumner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/fe34132d-badf-55cc-9c18-eaa4de4dae2a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/fe34132d-badf-55cc-9c18-eaa4de4dae2a'}, {'abstract': '“Birding Bob” knows how to find the birds of New York City. But some people aren’t happy about how he does it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/25/opinion/bob-of-the-park-new-york-birders.html', 'snippet': '“Birding Bob” knows how to find the birds of New York City. But some people aren’t happy about how he does it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you grab binoculars and head to Central Park in New York, you may see a warbler, a robin and Robert DeCandido, also known as “Birding Bob.” If you can’t spot him, you’ll definitely hear him. Among dedicated birders, some consider his use of recorded bird calls a disturbance to birds and bird-watchers alike, while others see him as an eager advocate for the natural world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ruffled Feathers Among the Birders of Central Park', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birdwatching', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-25T19:04:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Sumner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sumner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/512a63d9-3efd-5073-8b50-f0d8f5841324', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/512a63d9-3efd-5073-8b50-f0d8f5841324'}, {'abstract': 'This discrimination  is real, and federal law should reflect that.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/25/opinion/caste-discrimination-us-federal-protection.html', 'snippet': 'This discrimination  is real, and federal law should reflect that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Caste is not well understood in the United States, even though it plays a significant role in the lives of Americans of South Asian descent. Two recent lawsuits make caste among the South Asian diaspora much more visible. They show that oppressed castes in the United States are doubly disadvantaged — by caste and race. Making caste a protected category under federal law will allow for the recognition of this double disadvantage.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/25/opinion/sunday/25Caste/25Caste-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/25/opinion/sunday/25Caste/25Caste-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/25/opinion/sunday/25Caste/25Caste-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/25/opinion/sunday/25Caste/25Caste-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/25/opinion/sunday/25Caste/25Caste-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/25/opinion/sunday/25Caste/25Caste-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/25/opinion/sunday/25Caste/25Caste-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Is Caste Inequality Still Legal in America?', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Caste Inequality Reaches Into America', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caste Systems', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bochasanwasi Akshar Purushottam Swaminarayan Sanstha (BAPS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cisco Systems Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-25T19:06:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Chakravartty and Ajantha Subramanian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chakravartty', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ajantha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Subramanian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5faed5f8-a431-575f-97f6-3746f8b80617', 'word_count': 959, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5faed5f8-a431-575f-97f6-3746f8b80617'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans have argued that the existing Justice Department and congressional investigations will address the assault. But they have strict limits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/25/us/politics/capitol-riot-investigations.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans have argued that the existing Justice Department and congressional investigations will address the assault. But they have strict limits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the Senate moves this week toward voting on the creation of a 9/11-style commission to investigate the Jan. 6 attack on the Capitol, Republicans have raised a series of arguments against it. They have objected to the inquiry’s scope, its length and even the process for hiring its staff.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': Non