oireann-ni-ghriofa.html', 'snippet': 'In “A Ghost in the Throat,” Doireann Ni Ghriofa combines essay, biography and autofiction in writing about (and translating) a passionate 18th-century lament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A woman once fell in love with a poem — a keening, a roaring — for a slain beloved. The 18th-century Irish noblewoman Eibhlin Dubh Ni Chonaill composed “Caoineadh Airt Ui Laoghaire” after her husband was murdered by a powerful British official. Arriving at the scene, Ni Chonaill, pregnant with their third child, drank handfuls of her husband’s blood. “My bright dove,” “my pleasure,” she called him in the poem, “my thousand bewilderments” — why hadn’t she been with him? She imagined her blouse catching the bullet in its pleats.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/26/books/25BOOKGHRIOFA-1/25BOOKGHRIOFA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 881, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/26/books/25BOOKGHRIOFA-1/25BOOKGHRIOFA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 881}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/26/books/25BOOKGHRIOFA-1/25BOOKGHRIOFA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 698, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/26/books/25BOOKGHRIOFA-1/25BOOKGHRIOFA-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1400, 'width': 954, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/26/books/25BOOKGHRIOFA-1/25BOOKGHRIOFA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/26/books/25BOOKGHRIOFA-1/25BOOKGHRIOFA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/26/books/25BOOKGHRIOFA-1/25BOOKGHRIOFA-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Irish Poet Looks Back Three Centuries to Find Obsession and Inspiration in Another', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding Inspiration in an Irish Lament', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'A Ghost in the Throat (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ni Ghriofa, Doireann', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ni Chonaill, Eibhlin Dubh', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-25T19:23:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Parul Sehgal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Parul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sehgal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0288c91-1af9-58e0-91ec-a677b326d357', 'word_count': 875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0288c91-1af9-58e0-91ec-a677b326d357'}, {'abstract': 'The visit sent a clear message that India’s powerful ruling party is becoming increasingly upset with the company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/25/technology/covid-india-twitter.html', 'snippet': 'The visit sent a clear message that India’s powerful ruling party is becoming increasingly upset with the company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The officers from India’s elite antiterror