tina Goldbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Haley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Willis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christiaan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Triebert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Stella', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}, {'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Byrd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 5}, {'firstname': 'Christina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 6}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/42c71030-043a-56f5-886a-8141c1e1fc59', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/42c71030-043a-56f5-886a-8141c1e1fc59'}, {'abstract': 'As it stretches its premise across a fourth season, the show may inadvertently be channeling our real-world paralysis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/26/magazine/the-handmaids-tale-feels-stuck-it-kind-of-works.html', 'snippet': 'As it stretches its premise across a fourth season, the show may inadvertently be channeling our real-world paralysis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a face Elisabeth Moss makes in “The Handmaid’s Tale” — the face she makes whenever Gilead gets her down. Actually, there are two faces, but they’re similar, fluctuating between defiant and resigned. The defiant version is grim and vacant, a dead horse taking another beating. The resigned version takes that and adds a smile — one that manages, through the tears, to communicate ruefulness, cynicism, contempt and the sheer relief of finally giving up. This is not to suggest that Moss’s range of expression is limited. It’s just that there aren’t that many ways for her character to feel about the patriarchal regime that enslaved her and stole her child.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-screenland/30mag-screenland-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-screenland/30mag-screenland-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-screenland/30mag-screenland-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-screenland/30mag-screenland-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-screenland/30mag-screenland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-screenland/30mag-screenland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-screenland/30mag-screenland-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Handmaid’s Tale’ Feels Stuck. It Kind of Works.', 'kicker': 'Screenland', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stand Still', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "The Handmaid's Tale (TV Program)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moss, Elisabeth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-26T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carina Chocano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chocano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/681517a0-583c-58c5-8c9b-06976acbf820', 'word_count': 1195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/681517a0-583c-58c5-8c9b-06976acbf820'}, {'abstract': 'Biden has less than two years before congressional elections could change everything. Is now really the time for compromise?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/26/opinion/biden-mcconnell-bipartisan-infrastructure.html', 'snippet': 'Biden has less than two years before congressional elections could change everything. Is now really the time for compromise?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The clock is ticking for President Biden. He’s got a choice to make: compromise with Republicans or forgo them to push his agenda through with fellow Democrats. He has emphasized bipartisanship, but we’re now just days away from his self-imposed deadline of Memorial Day to strike a deal with Republicans on his infrastructure package. While negotiations continue, the parties are deadlocked on the size of the bill. It’s perhaps not surprising, given that this month the Senate minority leader, Mitch McConnell, said that “100 percent of our focus is on stopping this new administration.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Republicans Are Very, Very Close to Driving Democracy Into a Ditch’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R III', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-26T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': "By ‘The Argument'", 'person': [], 'organization': "The Argument'"}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6e33ac5-76e7-5135-af6f-73559a71bdd6', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6e33ac5-76e7-5135-af6f-73559a71bdd6'}, {'abstract': 'Take a fresh look at the people, places and things in your life. Now snap a photo. It could be a building you haven’t noticed before, a tree in your yard, children playing or your pet. Fill out the form at the end of this article to share your pictures with us!', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/26/well/gratitude-photo.html', 'snippet': '', 'lead_paragraph': 'Take a fresh look at the people, places and things in your life. Now snap a photo. It could be a building you haven’t noticed before, a tree in your yard, children playing or your pet. Fill out the form at the end of this article to share your pictures with us!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/well/challenge-awe/challenge-awe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/17/well/challenge-awe/challenge-awe-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/well/challenge-awe/challenge-awe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/well/challenge-awe/challenge-awe-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/well/challenge-awe/challenge-awe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/17/well/challenge-awe/challenge-awe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/well/challenge-awe/challenge-awe-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Day 8: Take a Gratitude Photo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Happiness', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-26T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1159145c-2c19-5559-a8ee-95cc09dd27e0', 'word_count': 692, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1159145c-2c19-5559-a8ee-95cc09dd27e0'}, {'abstract': 'The jackfruit is perfect for a meatless meal, especially this spicy and tangy sabzi from West Bengal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/26/magazine/jackfruit-sabzi-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'The jackfruit is perfect for a meatless meal, especially this spicy and tangy sabzi from West Bengal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Romy Gill didn’t work with canned jackfruit until she started research for her cookbook, “Zaika: Vegan Recipes From India.” Gill, a chef who was raised in Burnpur, West Bengal, had never really needed to: The fruit grew wild around her home, along with pomegranates, mangoes and guava. Fresh jackfruits look like gigantic, scaly lumps — a family of dragons asleep in the branches. A single fruit can reach 100 pounds, and even the small ones tend to be heavy and unwieldy. “It’s very tough when you cut it down fresh; it’s a lot of work,” she says. Every time Gill’s mother and her friends picked one, they cut it up and shared the fruit among themselves, working together, leaving the rest to keep ripening on the tree.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-eat/30mag-eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-eat/30mag-eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-eat/30mag-eat-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 770, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-eat/30mag-eat-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1540, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-eat/30mag-eat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-eat/30mag-eat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-eat/30mag-eat-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The 100-Pound Fruit That Vegans Love', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '100 Pounds: The jackfruit is perfect for a vegan meal, especially in this spicy and tangy sabzi from West Bengal. ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veganism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gujarat State (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-26T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tejal Rao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tejal', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57571e31-769f-555f-aa95-a3f7d72eebb9', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57571e31-769f-555f-aa95-a3f7d72eebb9'}, {'abstract': 'Don’t let the weight-loss industry shame you into thinking “back to normal” means a return to calorie counting and appetite suppressant lollipops.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/26/opinion/dieting-covid-weight-gain.html', 'snippet': 'Don’t let the weight-loss industry shame you into thinking “back to normal” means a return to calorie counting and appetite suppressant lollipops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the pandemic has raged, we have been told to sequester ourselves to stay well and safeguard others. For many of us, that has meant living a more housebound life than normal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Body Survived a Pandemic. Don’t Punish It With Diet Fads.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-opinionvideo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-26T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tala Schlossberg and Lindsay Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tala', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schlossberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Lindsay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e385ac1-95a6-5777-889f-65357d6e2252', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e385ac1-95a6-5777-889f-65357d6e2252'}, {'abstract': 'Using self-mesmerism I felt overtaken on a cellular level by a serene form of concentration. I began to accumulate pages and finish my projects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/26/magazine/productivity-self-mesmerism.html', 'snippet': 'Using self-mesmerism I felt overtaken on a cellular level by a serene form of concentration. I began to accumulate pages and finish my projects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One thing I knew as an aspiring writer was that I was supposed to sit in front of a page for more than 10 minutes. I could not. I had grown up in Colombia during a violent time in the country’s history; my family and I had fled, but I suffered from PTSD. Fear had worked its way under my skin. I wrote a sentence, then questioned whether my surroundings were safe. I got up to check the locks, turn every available light on. The writing came a sentence at a time, but I could hardly finish anything. Even so, I loved writing and longed to do it in spite of personal distress. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-LOR/30mag-LOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 439, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-LOR/30mag-LOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 439}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-LOR/30mag-LOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 749, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-LOR/30mag-LOR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1499, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-LOR/30mag-LOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-LOR/30mag-LOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/magazine/30mag-LOR/30mag-LOR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Centuries-Old Trick Will Unlock Your Productivity', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Self-Mesmerism ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hypnosis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Productivity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-26T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ingrid Rojas Contreras', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ingrid', 'middlename': 'Rojas', 'lastname': 'Contreras', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8015d8a-60b8-5739-9ccd-2dde0e681761', 'word_count': 940, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8015d8a-60b8-5739-9ccd-2dde0e681761'}, {'abstract': 'Puberty and perimenopause are a heady combination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/26/parenting/menopause-perimenopause-puberty.html', 'snippet': 'Puberty and perimenopause are a heady combination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tamara Tiska, 48, is a single mother of a 13-year-old son, and they’re both going through hormonal transitions; she’s in perimenopause and he’s in puberty. The past year of Covid isolation in Watertown, Mass., has been difficult for them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/26/multimedia/26PAR-NL-MENOPAUSE-PUBERTY/26PAR-NL-MENOPAUSE-PUBERTY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': '