rticle', 'news_desk': 'Parenting', 'section_name': 'Parenting', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Grose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5852054f-e861-5d8c-9015-419ffa2d086e', 'word_count': 964, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5852054f-e861-5d8c-9015-419ffa2d086e'}, {'abstract': 'George Floyd was killed by a police officer one year ago. His death galvanized a nation. How much do you think has changed since?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/26/learning/how-much-have-you-and-your-community-changed-since-george-floyds-death.html', 'snippet': 'George Floyd was killed by a police officer one year ago. His death galvanized a nation. How much do you think has changed since?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On May 25, 2020, George Floyd was killed when a white police officer knelt on his neck for more than nine agonizing minutes. His death sparked an uprising for racial justice nearly unparalleled in American history, and many believed it might be a turning point in the way Americans confront issues of race and racism.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/21/opinion/21OPN-onsite-final/21OPN-onsite-final-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/21/opinion/21OPN-onsite-final/21OPN-onsite-final-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/21/opinion/21OPN-onsite-final/21OPN-onsite-final-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't