}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be6064b4-c6c7-57d8-9fb2-2b0fc30f448b', 'word_count': 1683, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be6064b4-c6c7-57d8-9fb2-2b0fc30f448b'}, {'abstract': "Here's why individualism may be our best trait.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/26/opinion/individualism-united-states-altruism.html', 'snippet': "Here's why individualism may be our best trait.", 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States is notable for its individualism. The results of several large surveys assessing the values held by the people of various nations consistently rank the United States as the world’s most individualist country. Individualism, as defined by behavioral scientists, means valuing autonomy, self-expression and the pursuit of personal goals rather than prioritizing the interests of the group — be it family, community or country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/opinion/27marsh-print/26marsh-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/27/opinion/27marsh-print/26marsh-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/opinion/27marsh-print/26marsh-4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/opinion/27marsh-print/26marsh-4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1600, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/opinion/27marsh-print/26marsh-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/27/opinion/27marsh-print/26marsh-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/opinion/27marsh-print/26marsh-4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Everyone Thinks Americans Are Selfish. They’re Wrong.', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'We Aren’t as Selfish as We Think', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Altruism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-26T09:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abigail Marsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abigail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2309f68-b0fa-5e98-a3a2-e3397e6aae2f', 'word_count': 898, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2309f68-b0fa-5e98-a3a2-e3397e6aae2f'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans sure seem to think so. They are not alone.\xa0', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/26/opinion/democrats-republicans-wokeness-cancel-culture.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans sure seem to think so. They are not alone.\xa0', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Republicans well know, Democrats are divided on a host of volatile racial, cultural and sexual issues.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/26/opinion/2