8c7b4c462a7'}, {'abstract': 'Important immune cells survive in the bone marrow of people who were infected with the virus or were inoculated against it, new research suggests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/26/health/coronavirus-immunity-vaccines.html', 'snippet': 'Important immune cells survive in the bone marrow of people who were infected with the virus or were inoculated against it, new research suggests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Immunity to the coronavirus lasts at least a year, possibly a lifetime, improving over time especially after vaccination, according to two new studies. The findings may help put to rest lingering fears that protection against the virus will be short-lived.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/science/26VIRUS-IMMUNITY1/26VIRUS-IMMUNITY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/27/science/26VIRUS-IMMUNITY1/26VIRUS-IMMUNITY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/science/26VIRUS-IMMUNITY1/26VIRUS-IMMUNITY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/science/26VIRUS-IMMUNITY1/26VIRUS-IMMUNITY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/science/26VIRUS-IMMUNITY1/26VIRUS-IMMUNITY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/27/science/26VIRUS-IMMUNITY1/26VIRUS-IMMUNITY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/science/26VIRUS-IMMUNITY1/26VIRUS-IMMUNITY1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Immunity to the Coronavirus May Persist for Years, Scientists Find', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Studies Show Immunity to Virus May Persist for Years', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-science', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antibodies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immune System', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bone Marrow', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature (Journal)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Moderna Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-26T17:03:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Apoorva Mandavilli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Apoorva', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandavilli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e159955-8b8c-5369-b186-13a332e24082', 'word_count': 1222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e159955-8b8c-5369-b186-13a332e24082'}, {'abstract': 'José Mauro’s first LP, originally released in 1970, became a cult classic. Far Out Recordings is now putting out its follow-up under very different circumstances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/26/arts/music/jose-mauro-a-viagem-das-horas.html', 'snippet': 'José Mauro’s first LP, originally released in 1970, became a cult classic. Far Out Recordings is now putting out its follow-up under very different circumstances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2016, the British record label Far Out Recordings reissued the debut album by José Mauro, a mysterious Brazilian singer and guitarist whose 1970 LP, “Obnoxius,” had become a cult classic in his home country and with the famed crate diggers Madlib, Floating Points and Gilles Peterson. The album’s press materials noted that the conditions of Mauro’s death, presumed to have occurred in the 1970s, were unexplained. Maybe he perished in an auto accident, or was killed by the military for making what they thought were protest songs.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/26mauro1/26mauro1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 827, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/26mauro1/26mauro1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 827}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/26mauro1/26mauro1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 743, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/26mauro1/26mauro1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1486, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/26mauro1/26mauro1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/