 the time, were playing in the driveway when an unfamiliar car pulled up. The driver emerged, picked up one of the kids’ bicycles and hurled it at a basketball hoop. Before peeling away, the stranger implored the children: “Tell your father he sucks!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-SPORTS/06SummerReading-SPORTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-SPORTS/06SummerReading-SPORTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-SPORTS/06SummerReading-SPORTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-SPORTS/06SummerReading-SPORTS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1423, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-SPORTS/06SummerReading-SPORTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-SPORTS/06SummerReading-SPORTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-SPORTS/06SummerReading-SPORTS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Game On! Great New Sports Books', 'kicker': 'SPORTS BOOKS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Two Sides of Glory: The 1986 Boston Red Sox in Their Own Words (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sherman, Erik (Author)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Glory Days: The Summer of 1984 and the 90 Days That Changed Sports and Culture Forever (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wertheim, L Jon', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Sidelined: Sports, Culture, and Being a Woman in America (Book)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DiCaro, Julie A (1973- )', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Fans: How Watching Sports Makes Us Happier, Healthier, and More Understanding (Book)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olmsted, Larry (Journalist)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Cheated: The Inside Story of the Astros Scandal and a Colorful History of Sign Stealing (Book)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martino, Andy (Journalist)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'KG: A to Z: An Uncensored Encyclopedia of Life, Basketball, and Everything in Between (Book)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garnett, Kevin', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ritz, David', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-27T13:55:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Swansburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Swansburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/704cbd41-ee19-5839-9226-2e1c0458a6c5', 'word_count': 2835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/704cbd41-ee19-5839-9226-2e1c0458a6c5'}, {'abstract': 'Mainstream publishers are fully embracing queer love stories, our columnist writes: “I would call it an embarrassment of riches but what it really is, of course, is pride.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/27/books/new-romance-novels.html', 'snippet': 'Mainstream publishers are fully embracing queer love stories, our columnist writes: “I would call it an embarrassment of riches but what it really is, of course, is pride.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Time was I could have covered every queer romance novel put out by mainstream publishers and still have had room to spare in this column. Small and independent presses have been nurturing L.G.B.T.Q. romance authors forever, and digital self-publishing opened up still more doors, but up until very recently, the big traditional houses had far more queer villains than queer romance leads.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-ROMANCE/06SummerReading-ROMANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-ROMANCE/06SummerReading-ROMANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-ROMANCE/06SummerReading-ROMANCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-ROMANCE/06SummerReading-ROMANCE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1311, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-ROMANCE/06SummerReading-ROMANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-ROMANCE/06SummerReading-ROMANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-ROMANCE/06SummerReading-ROMANCE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sweet, Sexy and Rebellious: Summer’s New Romance Novels', 'kicker': 'ROMANCE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'One Last Stop (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McQuiston, Casey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'How to Find a Princess (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cole, Alyssa (Author)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Companion (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ottoman, EE', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hard Sell (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lin, Hudson', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Intimacy Experiment (Book)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Danan, Rosie', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Wisteria Society of Lady Scoundrels (Book)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holton, India', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sebastian, Cat', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Queer Principles of Kit Webb (Book)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-27T13:55:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Olivia Waite', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Olivia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waite', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d77e7a2-1a9c-50e1-9d74-688318b68fab', 'word_count': 2376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d77e7a2-1a9c-50e1-9d74-688318b68fab'}, {'abstract': 'From funny women to Yo-Yo Ma, self-reflection to civil rights, there’s something in the queue for everyone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/27/books/new-audiobooks.html', 'snippet': 'From funny women to Yo-Yo Ma, self-reflection to civil rights, there’s something in the queue for everyone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was only recently that I discovered the joy to be found in an audiobook-fueled road trip. For the longest time, books seemed too evocative for car rides, too absorbing to serve as mere accompaniment to a scenic journey. But then, around two years ago, I found myself in Chile, exhausted by a string of flight delays and facing a long drive through the night. Trusting an algorithm to find something to keep me awake, I downloaded “The Lost City of Z,” David Grann’s gripping tale of the obsessive, swashbuckling Victorian explorer Percy Fawcett.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multi