n the cookbook or lifestyle world, and you’ll most likely discover a complicated relationship with the concept “aspirational,” that magical space where content is both accessible and unique. It’s a balancing act: too accessible and no one’s learning anything; too unique and you run the risk of alienating people. (“Too much time!” “Too many steps!” “Too hard to find that ingredient!” “Too pricey!”) Is this a problem that requires a conference at Davos? No. But it does make the people doing it well shine brightly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-COOKING/06SummerReading-COOKING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-COOKING/06SummerReading-COOKING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-COOKING/06SummerReading-COOKING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-COOKING/06SummerReading-COOKING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1475, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-COOKING/06SummerReading-COOKING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/06/06/books/review/06SummerReading-COOKING/06SummerReading-COOKING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, 