'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bove, Carol', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zwirner, David, Gallery', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Remington, Deborah', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starr, Craig F, Gallery', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bortolami LLC', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hough, James Yaya', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JTT Gallery (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-27T14:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f07cef85-3dd4-5ab1-946e-2a3fb0c98fd6', 'word_count': 1216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f07cef85-3dd4-5ab1-946e-2a3fb0c98fd6'}, {'abstract': 'The unrivaled Art Preserve in Sheboygan, Wis., opening soon, is collecting and showing artist-built environments found along rural byways, in city lofts — and even at Manhattan’s Chelsea Hotel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/27/arts/design/Art-Preserve-Sheboygan.html', 'snippet': 'The unrivaled Art Preserve in Sheboygan, Wis., opening soon, is collecting and showing artist-built environments found along rural byways, in city lofts — and even at Manhattan’s Chelsea Hotel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHEBOYGAN, Wis. — Charles Smith preaches with sculpture, hundreds of hip-height figures that he’s been reworking, repainting and rearranging for decades, first at a small house in Aurora, Ill., and now at his homestead in Hammond, La. Every time this self-taught artist repositions his work he testifies anew to the unfolding history of racial violence in the United States, connecting it to personal traumas, including what he believes was the racially motivated murder of his father when he was 14, and his own combat experiences in Vietnam.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/arts/30folkart-museum-12/merlin_187225317_54ff6e05-ef31-4107-94e5-57f7db70d27e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/30/arts/30folkart-museum-12/merlin_187225317_54ff6e05-ef31-4107-94e5-57f7db70d27e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 840}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/arts/30folkart-museum-12/merlin_187225317_54ff6e05-ef31-4107-94e5-57f7db70d27e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 732, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/arts/30folkart-museum-12/merlin_187225317_54ff6e05-ef31-4107-94e5-57f7db70d27e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1463, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/arts/30folkart-museum-12/30folkart-museum-12-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/30/arts/30folkart-museum-12/30folkart-museum-12-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/30/arts/30folkart-museum-12/30folkart-museum-12-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rescuing Artists of Vision',