-established College of Fine Arts in honor of the actor and alumnus Chadwick Boseman, university officials said on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/us/27xp-howar-image/27xp-howar-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/27/us/27xp-howar-image/27xp-howar-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/us/27xp-howar-image/27xp-howar-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/us/27xp-howar-image/27xp-howar-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/us/27xp-howar-image/27xp-howar-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/27/us/27xp-howar-image/27xp-howar-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/us/27xp-howar-image/27xp-howar-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Howard University Renames College of Fine Arts After Chadwick Boseman', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Howard University to Honor Boseman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historically Black Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Organizational', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Howard University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boseman, Chadwick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boseman, Chadwick A, College of Fine Arts (Howard University)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iger, Robert A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-27T14:07:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Express', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Derrick Bryson Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Derrick', 'middlename': 'Bryson', 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/930421fe-e9b6-5140-a3e9-67cdad623b30', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/930421fe-e9b6-5140-a3e9-67cdad623b30'}, {'abstract': 'In her first show at Pace, an artist driven by curiosity and a penchant for the absurd tries to understand the world. The results are touching and sometimes hilarious.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/27/arts/design/nina-katchadourian-pace-artist.html', 'snippet': 'In her first show at Pace, an artist driven by curiosity and a penchant for the absurd tries to understand the world. The results are touching and sometimes hilarious.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nina Katchadourian is a sculptor, a printmaker, a photographer, a performance artist, a video artist, a sound artist — but more than any of those things she is an artist with a voracious curiosity and a marathoner’s stamina when it comes to running with an idea. In her first show at Pace Gallery, “Cumulus,” she offers up seven projects that are witty, sometimes even guffaw-inducing. But don’t let that fool you: Underneath the playfulness lurk some pretty fundamental questions about how we organize knowledge to make sense of our past and present.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/27nina-review-2/merlin_188257038_87e73ef4-fbf5-4432-b32e-7469d12a285d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/27nina-review-2/merlin_188257038_87e73ef4-fbf5-4432-b32e-7469d12a285d-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/27nina-review-2/merlin_188257038_87e73ef4-fbf5-4432-b32e-7469d12a285d-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/27nina-review-2/merlin_188257038_87e73ef4-fbf5-4432-b32e-7469d12a285d-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/27nina-review-2/27nina-review-2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/27nina-review-2/27nina-review-2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/27nina-review-2/27nina-review-2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nina Katchadourian’s Eccentric Existentialism', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Pick', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Eccentric Existentialism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Armenians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Katchadourian, Nina (1968- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pace Gallery', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Personal Profile', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-27T14:21:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': "By Aruna D'Souza", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aruna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "D'Souza", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/80ff74cf-51aa-54bb-adfd-c34fab4abf55', 'word_count': 1048, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80ff74cf-51aa-54bb-adfd-c34fab4abf55'}, {'abstract': 'With a survey in Europe and stark new sculptures in New York, he is bringing to the fore darker, more personal themes. “I’m an undertaker,” he said. “I don’t do the uplift thing.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/27/arts/design/arthur-jafa-gladstone-love-message-video.html', 'snippet': 'With a survey in Europe and stark new sculptures in New York, he is bringing to the fore darker, more personal themes. “I’m an undertaker,” he said. “I don’t do the uplift thing.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2019, Arthur Jafa won the Golden Lion award for best artist in the Venice Biennale for “The White Album.” A collage of found and original video, it mapped the psychology of Black-white relations in America today — the brutality, awkwardness and sometimes care. “Just as the film critiques a moment fraught with violence, in tenderly portraying the artist’s friends and family, it also speaks to our capacity for love,” the jury concluded.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/26arthurjafa-11NEW/26arthurjafa-11NEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/26arthurjafa-11NEW/26arthurjafa-11NEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/26arthurjafa-11NEW/26arthurjafa-11NEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/26arthurjafa-11NEW/26arthurjafa-11NEW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/26arthurjafa-11NEW/26arthurjafa-11NEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/26arthurjafa-11NEW/26arthurjafa-11NEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/arts/26arthurjafa-11NEW/26arthurjafa-11NEW-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At His Moment of Triumph, Arthur Jafa Is Looking for Trouble', 'kicker': None, 'co