 'word_count': 1183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9407ea2-712e-51ff-ac42-05ab17814d75'}, {'abstract': 'Suggested reading from critics and editors at The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/27/books/review/10-new-books-we-recommend-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Suggested reading from critics and editors at The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The approach of Memorial Day means that a lot of people are nearing the end of a very weird school year — one that started with learning via computer screen and is concluding with a fitful return to something like normal, with proms and in-person graduation ceremonies, masked or not. But the end of school doesn’t need to mean the end of learning. We have a full curriculum of books on offer this week, from geometry (“Shape,” by Jordan Ellenberg) to U.S. history (“King Richard,” by Michael Dobbs) to science (“The Premonition,” by Michael Lewis) to psychology (“Think Again,” by Adam Grant). There’s a music memoir by Brandi Carlile and, in fiction, a collection of updated folk tales as well as novels set in Brazil, Japan, London and New York City.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/books/27RecBooks/27RecBooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 297, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/27/books/27RecBooks/27RecBooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 297}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/books/27RecBooks/27RecBooks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/books/27RecBooks/27RecBooks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1349, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/books/27RecBooks/27RecBooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/27/books/27RecBooks/27RecBooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/27/books/27RecBooks/27RecBooks-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '10 New Books We Recommend This Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Staff Picks From the Book Review', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Shape: The Hidden Geometry of Information, Biology, Strategy, Democracy, and Everything Else (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ellenberg, Jordan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Richard Milhous', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'King Richard: Nixon and Watergate -- An American Tragedy (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dobbs, Michael (1950- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Broken Horses (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carlile, Brandi', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Decagon House Murders (Book)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ayatsuji, Yukito', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wong, Ho-Ling (Translator)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Ghosts of New York (Book)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Jim (1963- )', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Love in Color: Mythical Tales From Around the World, Retold (Book)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Babalola, Bolu', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Premonition: A Pandemic Story (Book)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Michael', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hot Stew (Book)', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mozley, Fiona', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'An Apprenticeship: Or The Book of Pleasures (Book)', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lispector, Clarice', 'rank': 21, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tobler, Stefan (Translator)', 'rank': 22, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Think Again: The Power of Knowing What You Don't Know (Book)", 'rank': 23, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grant, Adam M', 'rank': 24, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-27T19:48:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/17f3c789-118d-52cc-b61c-f88769657f7a', 'word_count': 1224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17f3c789-118d-52cc-b61c-f88769657f7a'}, {'abstract': 'As restaurants struggled last year, many chefs survived by selling food directly to customers, an age-old practice that is now shaping the future of hospitality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/27/t-magazine/restaurants-chefs-instagram.html', 'snippet': 'As restaurants struggled last year, many chefs survived by selling food directly to customers, an age-old practice that is now shaping the future of hospitality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last September, the chef Jennifer Kim did something that would have been unthinkable a year prior: Faced with the possibility of an ongoing shutdown as cases of Covid-19 rose in Chicago, and the risk of her staff getting sick, she closed the doors of Passerotto, the successful Italian-inflected Korean restaurant she’d opened in the city’s Andersonville neighborhood in 2018. “We had to make the decision to put people over profits,” she said. But she hardly sat idle. Instead, she began offering ready-made dishes and do-it-yourself meal kits, ordered via a website and prepped by her and others in underground kitchens, shared kitchen spaces and even homes around Chicago. On the day of pickup, Kim and the vendors whose wares were part of the boxes collectively put together the orders in storefronts or restaurants where customers could stop by and take home their food. “The advantage of having no dedicated staff and everyone being their own bosses is that it’s a decentralized, fluid and completely collaborative project,” Kim says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/20/t-magazine/20tmag-restaurants-slide-K013/20tmag-restaurants-slide-K013-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 464, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/20/t-magazine/20tmag-restaurants-slide-K013/20tmag-restaurants-slide-K013-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 464}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/20/t-magazine/20tmag-restaurants-slide-K013/20tmag-restaurants-slide-K013-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 792, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/20/t-magazine/20tmag-restaurants-slide-K013/20tmag-restaurants-slide-K013-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1584, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/20/t-magazine/20tmag-restaurants-slide-K013/20tmag-restaurants-slide-K013-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/20/t-magazine/20tmag-restaurants-slide-K013/20tmag-restaurants-slide-K013-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/20/t-magazine/20tmag-restaurants-slide-K013/20tmag-restaurants-slide-K013-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Benefits of Ordering Dinner From Instagram', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Trucks and Vendors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-27T20:08:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Korsha Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Korsha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/330cae1e-a291-5f6e-b60a-df729fdb5e20', 'word_count': 1428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/330cae1e-a291-5f6e-b60a-df729fdb5e20'}, {'abstract': 'She and her partner, Barbara Gittings, were on the front lines long before Stonewall, and Ms. Lahusen photographed protests during the movement’s earliest days.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/27/us/kay-tobin-lahusen-gay-rights-activist-and-photographer-dies-at-91.html', 'snippet': 'She and her partner, Barbara Gittings, were on the front lines long before Stonewall, and Ms. Lahusen photographed protests during the movement’s earliest days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kay Tobin Lahusen, a prominent gay rights activist whose photographs documented the movement’s earliest days and depicted lesbians who were out when they were virtually absent from popular culture, died on Wednesday in West Chester, Pa. She was 91.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/obituaries/27lahusen/27lahusen-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/28/obituaries/27lahusen/27lahusen-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/obituaries/27lahusen/27lahusen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/obituaries/27lahusen/27lahusen-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1369, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/obituaries/27lahusen/27lahusen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard',