elf-compassion break. Ask yourself, “What do I need right now?” Then, do something nice for yourself: Take a walk or a hot bath. Call a friend for support. Adopt this mantra: “I’m going to be kind to myself. I accept myself as I am.” Being good to ourselves makes us more likely to adopt healthy behaviors. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/well/challenge-break/challenge-break-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/17/well/challenge-break/challenge-break-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/well/challenge-break/challenge-break-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/well/challenge-break/challenge-break-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/well/challenge-break/challenge-break-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/17/well/challenge-break/challenge-break-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/17/well/challenge-break/challenge-break-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Day 10: Give Yourself a Break!', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Empathy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-28T09:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89a20ec9-8137-5eb2-9c25-2c66b8deaceb', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89a20ec9-8137-5eb2-9c25-2c66b8deaceb'}, {'abstract': 'Stephen S. Miller, a cabaret performer, is used to the limelight, but when it came time to getting engaged, the more introverted Brian Geldin took center stage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/28/style/stephen-s-miller-brian-geldin-wedding.html', 'snippet': 'Stephen S. Miller, a cabaret performer, is used to the limelight, but when it came time to getting engaged, the more introverted Brian Geldin took center stage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s usually rare that anyone upstages Stephen S. Miller, or Mama Rose as he’s known in some corners of the New York theater world. Outgoing and charismatic, he tends to be center of attention wherever he goes, even when he’s not wielding a microphone as a cabaret performer. By contrast, Brian Geldin, is more of an introvert. “I have always been more of a tight-lipped, dry sense of humor kind of guy,” he said. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '