riginal': 'By Peter Libbey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Libbey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9a61fa8-2829-53db-a249-983e68b4678b', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9a61fa8-2829-53db-a249-983e68b4678b'}, {'abstract': 'Americans may not need to achieve that goal in order to escape the Covid-19 pandemic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/28/opinion/herd-immunity-covid-us.html', 'snippet': 'Americans may not need to achieve that goal in order to escape the Covid-19 pandemic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Half of Americans have now received at least one dose of a Covid-19 vaccine, and with children ages 12 to 15 now eligible for immunizations, the United States appears to be getting the coronavirus pandemic under control. But despite the tremendous progress, it’s still not clear that the nation will ever truly reach the herd immunity threshold —\xa0the point at which enough people in a population are immune to a pathogen to limit its spread.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The U.S. May Never Hit the Herd Immunity Threshold. That’s OK.', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disease Rates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Reopenings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-28T09:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erin A. Mordecai, Mallory J. Harris and Marc Lipsitch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erin', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Mordecai', '