ganization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a270cd1-ec6f-5602-806e-35ef896549e5', 'word_count': 935, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a270cd1-ec6f-5602-806e-35ef896549e5'}, {'abstract': 'The restaurant is a culinary landmark in San Francisco, but its history as a space for gay visibility is little known.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/28/dining/billy-west-zuni-cafe.html', 'snippet': 'The restaurant is a culinary landmark in San Francisco, but its history as a space for gay visibility is little known.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2013 Judy Rodgers, the 57-year-old chef of Zuni Café in San Francisco, yielded at last to the rare appendix cancer she’d struggled with for more than a year. The many published tributes to Ms. Rodgers celebrated the urgent beauty in her deceptively simple dishes: the way Zuni’s roast chicken, house-cured anchovies and Caesar salad were woven into memories of perfect meals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/dining/28zuni1/merlin_188259132_55c87413-9fb6-41df-83cc-10ffe026314f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 942, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/28/dining/28zuni1/merlin_188259132_55c87413-9fb6-41df-83cc-10ffe026314f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 942}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/dining/28zuni1/merlin_188259132_55c87413-9fb6-41df-83cc-10ffe026314f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 653, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/28/dining/28zuni1/merlin_188259132_55c87413-9fb6-41df-83cc-10ffe026314f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1306, 'subType': 'superJumbo', '