 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e33898b-3120-5cb6-b4af-5f9d379bb9f7', 'word_count': 1017, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e33898b-3120-5cb6-b4af-5f9d379bb9f7'}, {'abstract': 'Sometimes a place is more than just a place; it can be a scene. Even the blankest backdrops, like a parking lot or a sun-baked freeway, can shimmer with cinematic potential. Four photographers showed us the movie moments that they found all over.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/28/arts/photographers-find-cinematic-moments-in-real-life.html', 'snippet': 'Sometimes a place is more than just a place; it can be a scene. Even the blankest backdrops, like a parking lot or a sun-baked freeway, can shimmer with cinematic potential. Four photographers showed us the movie moments that they found all over.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Jake Michaels began shooting around Los Angeles, he noticed how the backdrop and spontaneous action within the frame combine to tell a story, and how those moments dissolve quickly. “That’s why I think it’s interesting to go back to a place several times,” Michaels said. “You can see life kind of cycling. You see from a static point of view how much life exists in that frame.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/02/arts/02the-take-jake1/merlin_186765162_758eabbd-f5fe-4636-bcab-685a8759c60a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/02/arts/02the-take-jake1/merlin_186765162_758eabbd-f5fe-4636-bcab-685a8759c60a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/02/arts/02the-take-jake1/merlin_186765162_758eabbd-f5fe-4636-bcab-685a8759c60a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}