78-72fe1e71433f', 'word_count': 848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c5f7b4a-b284-5feb-b178-72fe1e71433f'}, {'abstract': 'The organizers of a major London exhibition wanted to put politics aside and showcase the country’s rich 5,000-year-old culture. But politics kept getting in the way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/31/arts/design/iran-ayatollah.html', 'snippet': 'The organizers of a major London exhibition wanted to put politics aside and showcase the country’s rich 5,000-year-old culture. But politics kept getting in the way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The board game is roughly 4,500 years old. Shaped like a bird of prey, it has holes running down its wings and chest, where the pieces were once positioned. It’s one of a few dozen ancient objects that were set to travel from the National Museum of Iran for a spectacular exhibition at the Victoria & Albert Museum here. But they never came.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/31/arts/31iran-installation1/merlin_188520978_0671cdac-b955-4db0-a565-1d3132df13c1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/31/arts/31iran-installation1/merlin_188520978_0671cdac-b955-4db0-a565-1d3132df13c1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/31/arts/31iran-installation1/merlin_188520978_0671cdac-b955-4db0-a565-1d3132df13c1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/31/arts/31iran-installation1/merlin_188520978_0671cdac-b955-4db0-a565-1d3132df13c1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1334, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/31/arts/31iran-installation1/31iran-installation1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/31/arts/31iran-installation1/31iran-installation1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/31/arts/31iran-installation1/31iran-installation1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking Beyond the Ayatollah to the Treasures of Iran', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Victoria and Albert Museum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Museum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aliabadi, Shirin (1973-2018)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'MacGregor, Neil (1946- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-05-31T13:14:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Farah Nayeri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Farah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nayeri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfb57646-c509-5247-9a20-2cbbeb39f7e7', 'word_count': 1205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfb57646-c509-5247-9a20-2cbbeb39f7e7'}, {'abstract': 'Maryland and Montana have passed the nation’s first laws limiting forensic genealogy, the method that found the Golden State Killer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/31/science/dna-police-laws.html', 'snippet': 'Maryland and Montana have passed the nation’s first laws limiting forensic genealogy, the method that found the Golden State Killer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New laws in Maryland and Montana are the first in the nation to restrict law enforcement’s use of genetic genealogy, the DNA matching technique that in 2018 identified the Golden State Killer, in an effort to ensure the genetic privacy of the accused and their relatives.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/science/00DNA-LAW1/merlin_187103118_53128e68-ed81-49fe-b009-544cceb6679e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/11/science/00DNA-LAW1/merlin_187103118_53128e68-ed81-49fe-b009-544cceb6679e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/science/00DNA-LAW1/merlin_187103118_53128e68-ed81-49fe-b009-544cceb6679e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/science/00DNA-LAW1/merlin_187103118_53128e68-ed81-49fe-b009-544cceb6679e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/11/science/00DNA-LAW1/00DNA-LAW1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/05/11/science/00DNA-LAW1/00DNA-LAW1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}